<name>ESCRS London 2026 — Dror's Guide</name>
<Folder><name>🎭 West End</name>
<Placemark><name>Hamilton (Victoria Palace Theatre) ★4.7</name><description>The cheapest big-show ticket in London: £10 lottery seats for every performance via the official app (note: the £12.50 standing-ticket scheme ended 5 Sep 2026, before your window).

💷 Lottery £10; standard seats vary by performance up to limited £500 premium; £12.50 standing scheme ended 5 Sep 2026
🕐 Perfs Mon-Sat 19:30; mats Thu &amp; Sat 14:30; dark Sun. Booking to 13 Mar 2027. ~2h45 incl 15-min interval
🚇 45 min · DLR Custom House→Canning Town → Jubilee to Green Park → Victoria line 1 stop to Victoria; theatre 2 min from station
📍 Victoria Palace Theatre, Victoria Street, London SW1E 5EA

Weekly lottery confirmed on the official site: enter via the official Hamilton app (TodayTix-powered); entries open Fri 00:01 and close Thu 13:00, drawn Thu afternoon for ALL of the following week's shows; winners buy 1-2 tickets at £10, claim fast when notified. To cover Sep 10-16 enter the draws closing Thu 3 Sep and Thu 10 Sep (enter from home before flying). Odds are long but free to enter both weeks. CORRECTION: the £12.50 standing scheme was tied to the Leslie Odom, Jr. run (3 Jul-5 Sep 2026, released Mondays 11:00) and has ENDED — no standing backup in your window unless a new scheme is announced; fallback is daily returns (official site says check daily, best availability midweek). 19:30 curtain is makeable after an 18:00 congress finish. UNVERIFIED: exact standard price range (~£23-£250).

https://hamiltonmusical.com/london/lottery/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1429,51.4965,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harry Potter and the Cursed Child (Palace Theatre) ★4.6</name><description>Your week is the LAST full week anywhere of the original two-part production (final perf 20 Sep 2026; one-part version opens 9 Oct 2026) — £40 for both parts via the Friday Forty lottery.

💷 Friday Forty £40 both parts (£20/part); normal from ~£36 per part, good seats £60-£100+/part
🕐 Two-part: Wed/Fri/Sat Part 1 14:00 + Part 2 19:00; Sun 13:00 + 18:00; dark Mon/Tue/Thu. Part 1 2h45, Part 2 2h35. Two-part run ends 20 Sep 2026; one-part version opens 9 Oct 2026
🚇 30-35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 5-min walk to Cambridge Circus
📍 Palace Theatre, 113 Shaftesbury Avenue, London W1D 5AY

Friday Forty confirmed on the official site: 40 tickets at £40 released weekly — enter in the TodayTix app Fridays 00:01-13:00, winners notified 13:00-17:00 same day (1h to claim), valid for the FOLLOWING week. Enter Fri 4 Sep (covers Fri 11-Sun 13) and Fri 11 Sep (covers the final week incl. Wed 16 Sep). Odds reality: heavily oversubscribed and the farewell weeks will be worse — treat as a bonus, not a plan. Schedule reality: both parts = matinee+evening in one day (same seats for consecutive perfs), so it only fits Wed 16 Sep (departure day) or by skipping a congress Sat/Sun block; paid seats and TKTS are the fallback. UNVERIFIED: advance price floor (~£36/part).

https://uk.harrypottertheplay.com/friday-forty/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1289,51.5133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>TKTS Booth, Leicester Square ★4.5</name><description>The official Society of London Theatre discount booth — genuine 25-50% off same-day and advance tickets, no scalpers, profits back into theatre.

💷 Discounted and full-price tickets, typically 25-50% off face on big musicals (stalls ~£35-£60); small per-ticket booking fee; card/cash/Theatre Tokens
🕐 Sep = regular hours: Mon-Sat 10:30-18:00, Sun 11:00-16:00 (summer extension ends 29 Aug)
🚇 35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 8-min walk down Charing Cross Rd
📍 The Clocktower Building, south side of Leicester Square (opposite Radisson Blu Edwardian Hampshire), London WC2H 7NA

Key hack for a congress schedule, confirmed on the official site: on-the-day prices are IDENTICAL online at officiallondontheatre.com/tkts, with new stock loaded 00:01 daily — check the board over breakfast at ExCeL and buy from your phone instead of queueing (e-tickets online, paper at the booth). Sells same-day plus advance tickets, so on free Thu 10 Sep you can sort the weekend. UNVERIFIED: the exact advance window (the old 'same day + next 2 days' rule is no longer stated on the site). Expect Wicked/Lion King/Mormon-tier shows regularly listed; Hamilton and Cursed Child rarely appear. Physical booth queue worst 12:00-15:00; arrive at 10:30 opening for best seat picks.

https://officiallondontheatre.com/ticket-booth/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1303,51.5098,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Book of Mormon (Prince of Wales Theatre) ★4.7</name><description>£25 same-day tickets via the TodayTix app for the West End's filthiest-funny musical — note the famous in-person £20 hat lottery is no longer advertised in 2026.

💷 TodayTix same-day tickets £25; Under-30s scheme £25; standard prices vary by performance (groups 10+ from £44)
🕐 Perfs Mon-Sat 19:30; mats Fri &amp; Sat 14:30; dark Sun. Booking to 23 Jan 2027
🚇 35-40 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 10-min walk via Leicester Square
📍 Prince of Wales Theatre, 31 Coventry Street, London W1D 6AS

CORRECTION: the celebrated in-person £20 box-office hat lottery is no longer advertised by the producers and no longer listed by day-seat trackers (Aug 2026) — don't build a plan around it. The current cheap route is £25 day tickets released same-day in the TodayTix app, first-come (typically 10:00) — grab during a morning coffee break at ExCeL; midweek easiest. Under-30s can sign up for £25 tickets on the official site. 19:30 curtain works after an 18:00 ExCeL finish; dark Sunday.

https://www.delfontmackintosh.co.uk/whats-on/the-book-of-mormon</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1322,51.5101,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>SIX the Musical (Vaudeville Theatre) ★4.6</name><description>The perfect post-congress show: 80 minutes, no interval, £25 same-day Rush — the six wives of Henry VIII as a pop concert.

💷 TodayTix Rush £25; normal from £34.50 (incl £1.50 restoration levy), premium ~£100+
🕐 Tue/Wed/Fri 20:00; Thu &amp; Sat 16:00 + 20:00; Sun 15:00 + 19:00; dark Mon. 80 min, no interval. Booking to Nov 2027
🚇 40 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 12-min walk via Charing Cross Rd and Strand
📍 Vaudeville Theatre, 404 Strand, London WC2R 0NH

Rush confirmed but at £25, not £30: unlock SIX in the TodayTix app, same-day tickets drop at 10:00 sharp, first-come — be refreshing at 09:59; midweek is very gettable. 80-minute runtime means the 20:00 curtain (Sun 19:00) puts you out ~21:25 with the Elizabeth line running well past midnight Mon-Sat — the lowest-effort theatre night of the week, with comfortable margin after an 18:00 congress finish. No Monday shows, so not an option on your lighter Sep 14.

https://sixthemusical.com/london/tickets/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1212,51.5105,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wicked (Apollo Victoria Theatre) ★4.6</name><description>London's longest-running blockbuster still does the Daily Dozen: a dozen seats at £29.50 released in the TodayTix app at 10:00 every performance day.

💷 Daily Dozen £29.50; Front Row £29.50 (Wed 10:00 release for following week); normal from £25 (Tue-Thu offer from £29.50) to ~£150+ premium
🕐 Perfs Tue-Sat 19:30; mats Wed, Sat &amp; Sun 14:30; dark Mon. ~2h45 incl 20-min interval
🚇 45 min · DLR Custom House→Canning Town → Jubilee to Green Park → Victoria line to Victoria; theatre opposite the station
📍 Apollo Victoria Theatre, 17 Wilton Road, London SW1V 1LG

Daily Dozen confirmed on the official FAQ: limited day seats at £29.50, no fees, released 10:00 on every performance day exclusively via the TodayTix app — they go fast: app open at 09:59, payment card pre-saved. Also confirmed: Front Row tickets at £29.50 released every Wednesday 10:00 for the FOLLOWING week — set an alarm Wed 9 Sep to cover your whole window. CORRECTION: dark MONDAY, not Sunday (Sunday has a 14:30 matinee) — so Wicked is not an option on your lighter Mon 14 Sep. Tue-Thu performances are the cheapest advance buys; Wicked appears at TKTS most days. 19:30 curtain fine after congress; same station area as Hamilton (Victoria), so pair strategies.

https://www.wickedthemusical.co.uk/book-tickets/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1423,51.495,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Cabaret at the Kit Kat Club (Playhouse Theatre) ★4.6</name><description>Immersive in-the-round Cabaret with the theatre rebuilt as a 1930s Berlin club — the £30 weekly lottery includes some of the best (table) seats in the house.

💷 Lottery £30; normal ~£35-£350+ (stage-side dining tables top the range)
🕐 Perfs Mon-Sat 19:30; mats Wed &amp; Sat 14:00; dark Sun (~2h45); arrive 60+ min early — pre-show club performances are part of the experience
🚇 40 min · DLR Custom House→Canning Town → Jubilee to Waterloo → 8-min walk over Hungerford Bridge
📍 Playhouse Theatre, Northumberland Avenue, London WC2N 5DE

Lottery mechanics confirmed: via TodayTix app, entries open Mondays 00:01 and close Wednesday 13:00, winners notified Wednesday afternoon with 30 minutes to claim £30 tickets — prizes include prime table seats normally £150+, the best value-multiple in the West End. Enter the week before you want to go. Casting of Skylar Astin and Sarah Hyland as incoming Emcee/Sally is confirmed; UNVERIFIED: exact takeover date (reported 21 Sep 2026) — either way your week catches the outgoing cast. Come at ~18:15 for the Prologue company in the bars — leaving congress at 18:00 sacrifices that, so this fits best on Thu 10 or Mon 14 Sep. Dark Sunday.

https://kitkat.club/tickets/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1237,51.507,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Disney's The Lion King (Lyceum Theatre) ★4.7</name><description>The easiest rush win of the big titles — £25 same-day TodayTix seats to the show whose opening puppetry sequence alone justifies the trip.

💷 TodayTix Rush £25; normal from ~£43 to ~£150
🕐 Perfs Tue-Sat 19:30; mats Wed &amp; Sat 14:30, Sun 14:30 (no Sun evening); dark Mon. Booking to 16 May 2027
🚇 40 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 13-min walk through Covent Garden
📍 Lyceum Theatre, 21 Wellington Street, London WC2E 7RQ

Rush confirmed: £25 same-day tickets in the TodayTix app (released morning of, first-come); with ~2,100 seats the Lyceum's rush survives minutes rather than seconds — realistic to snag from a congress coffee queue, especially Tue-Thu. Bonus route confirmed: Disney's 'Magical Mondays' deal drops Mondays 12:00 on the official site (max 2 tickets). Restricted-view for some rush seats; the Circle overhang matters less here since the animals parade through the stalls aisles. Also a TKTS regular at ~30-45% off. Dark Monday — so not an option on your lighter Sep 14. Venue advises arriving 60-90 min early for security.

https://www.thelionking.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1201,51.5117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Stranger Things: The First Shadow (Phoenix Theatre) ★4.5</name><description>Olivier-winning Netflix prequel play with the most jaw-dropping stagecraft in London — closing 27 Dec 2026, £25 Rush and genuinely cheap advance seats.

💷 TodayTix Rush £25; advance from £25; peak seats £100+
🕐 Perfs Tue-Sat 19:00; mats Fri &amp; Sat 13:00; Sun 15:00 matinee only; dark Mon; 3h incl interval. West End run ends 27 Dec 2026 (confirmed)
🚇 30-35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Tottenham Court Rd + 3-min walk
📍 Phoenix Theatre, 110 Charing Cross Road, London WC2H 0JP

£25 Rush in the TodayTix app day-of (confirmed on day-seat trackers, Aug 2026); midweek odds good since advance prices genuinely start at £25 — booking a cheap upper-level seat ahead is the zero-stress option. Warning for the congress week: 19:00 curtain + 3h runtime means leaving ExCeL at 18:00 gets you there ~18:40 — tight but doable via Elizabeth line; the theatre is 3 min from Tottenham Court Rd station, closest walk of any show on this list. Sunday's only show is a 15:00 matinee (clashes with congress hours). Recommended 12+. Works without deep knowledge of the series, better if you've seen it.

https://uk.strangerthingsonstage.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.129,51.5136,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>🛍️ Markets</name>
<Placemark><name>Borough Market ★4.6</name><description>London's flagship food market — top-tier produce, cheese, oysters and dense street food under Victorian railway viaducts by London Bridge.

💷 Free entry; street-food mains £7-12, oysters ~£3.50 each, Bread Ahead doughnuts ~£4
🕐 Tue-Fri 10:00-17:00, Sat 9:00-17:00, Sun 10:00-16:00; closed Mon
🚇 30 min · Custom House DLR → Canning Town → Jubilee line to London Bridge, 4-min walk
📍 8 Southwark Street, London SE1 1TL

No booking, just go; arrive before 11:30 or after 14:30 to dodge peak queues. Order: Kappacasein raclette or cheese toastie, Richard Haward's oysters, Bread Ahead doughnuts. Full stall lineup Tue-Sat; Sunday runs smaller. Closes too early (17:00) for post-congress evenings — this is a daytime mission. Hours re-verified on the official site Aug 2026.

https://boroughmarket.org.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.091,51.5055,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Greenwich Market ★4.5</name><description>Covered crafts-antiques-and-food market inside the Greenwich World Heritage core — the closest market to his hotel and open all 7 days of his stay.

💷 Free entry; street-food £6-10, crafts/prints from ~£10
🕐 Daily 10:00-17:30 (no seasonal closures in September)
🚇 30-35 min · Custom House DLR toward Bank → change Poplar → Lewisham-branch DLR to Cutty Sark, 3-min walk
📍 Greenwich Market (off King William Walk), London SE10 9HZ

~120 stalls at weekend peak. Lowest-effort market win of the trip: pair with Cutty Sark, the Royal Observatory meridian line and the Thames foot tunnel for an easy half-day — ideal for light Mon Sep 14. UNVERIFIED: the traditional fixed rota (antiques Tue/Thu/Fri, designer-makers Wed + weekends) is no longer published on the official site, which now lists traders per-day via a filter — check the online guide for the exact day's mix. The 17:30 close rules out post-congress visits; river is between hotel and market, hence the DLR change at Poplar.

https://greenwichmarket.london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.009,51.4816,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Old Spitalfields Market ★4.6</name><description>Victorian covered market with a modern food hall, trader stalls and a serious Thursday antiques day — the only major market open into the evening.

💷 Free entry; food-hall mains £8-14, antiques from £5 to serious money
🕐 Mon-Wed &amp; Fri 10:00-20:00, Thu 8:00-18:00, Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 10:00-17:00
🚇 25 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool Street (~9 min), 6-min walk
📍 16 Horner Square, London E1 6EW

The one market that works after congress: open to 20:00 Mon/Tue/Wed/Fri and only 25 min door-to-door. Thursday antiques dealers set up from 8:00 — Victorian jewellery, mid-century pieces, cameras, vinyl. Eat: Dumpling Shack's shengjianbao in the food hall. 10-min walk to Brick Lane for a combined evening. Hours and Thursday antiques market re-verified on the official site Aug 2026.

https://oldspitalfieldsmarket.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0748,51.5196,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Maltby Street Market ★4.6</name><description>Compact foodie market squeezed into Bermondsey railway arches — locals' answer to Borough, with a Friday-night session that fits a post-congress evening.

💷 Free entry; dishes £8-12, craft beer £6-7
🕐 Fri 17:30-21:00, Sat 10:00-17:00, Sun 11:00-16:00; closed Mon-Thu
🚇 40 min · Custom House DLR → Canning Town → Jubilee to London Bridge, then 15-min walk via Tower Bridge Rd
📍 Ropewalk, Maltby Street, London SE1 3PA

Running since 2010 in the Ropewalk, a narrow alley of ~30 arches and stalls — rammed by 13:00 on Saturdays, so on a weekend go at opening. The Friday 17:30-21:00 session means he can leave ExCeL at 18:00 and still get a full street-food dinner — session times re-verified on the official site Aug 2026. Saturday bonus if skipping congress: adjacent Bermondsey Beer Mile taprooms and free White Cube gallery.

https://www.maltbystreetmarket.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0755,51.4989,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Columbia Road Flower Market ★4.6</name><description>A Victorian shopping street buried in cut flowers every Sunday — barrow traders shouting prices, one of London's great free spectacles.

💷 Free; flower bunches £5-10, houseplants £3-15 — traders slash prices (roughly half) after ~14:00
🕐 Sun 8:00-~15:00 ONLY ('8am til 3ish' per the official site); the street's indie shops also open Sundays
🚇 35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Whitechapel → Overground 2 stops to Hoxton, 8-min walk
📍 Columbia Road, London E2 7RG

Decide if it's worth a skipped Sunday-morning session — as a spectacle it's unique, and 8:00-9:30 is the calm window with the best stock. Cash speeds up barrow purchases. It closes ~15:00, so no post-congress option exists. Pairs with Brick Lane (15-20-min walk south) for one East End Sunday-morning loop.

https://columbiaroad.info/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0693,51.5289,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Brick Lane Market (Truman Brewery) ★4.5</name><description>Sunday street-market sprawl through the Bangladeshi East End — vintage, records, street food, street art and the 24-hour Beigel Bake.

💷 Free; salt-beef beigel ~£7, street-food dishes £7-10, vintage from £10
🕐 Full street market Sun ~10:00-18:00; Backyard craft market Sat 11:00-18:00 &amp; Sun 10:00-18:00; Upmarket food hall Mon-Sat 11:00-18:00, Sun 10:00-18:00; Brick Lane Vintage Market daily
🚇 30 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool Street, 12-min walk via Brushfield St
📍 Old Truman Brewery, 91 Brick Lane, London E1 6QL

The famous version is Sunday-only, but the fallback is strong: Beigel Bake at 159 Brick Lane is 24-hour, so the salt-beef beigel works after any congress day, and the Truman Brewery's Brick Lane Vintage Market now runs 7 days (Mon-Fri 11:00-18:30) alongside the street-art corridor (Hanbury St). If he does the Columbia Road Sunday dash, this is the natural second stop. Market hours re-verified on the Truman Brewery site Aug 2026.

https://www.trumanbrewery.com/markets</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0716,51.5218,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Camden Market ★4.6</name><description>Britain's most-visited market: goth-punk heritage, ~1,000 stalls and canal-side food yards — touristy, but the Regent's Canal setting delivers.

💷 Free entry; street-food £8-12
🕐 Daily 10:00-19:00 incl. bank holidays; Hawley Wharf food halls Mon-Sun 11:30-23:00
🚇 45 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Camden Town, 5-min walk
📍 Camden Lock Place, London NW1 8AF

Avoid weekends — it drowns in tourists. A late-afternoon Monday run gets shopping before the 19:00 close, then dinner at Hawley Wharf (food halls to 23:00) or KERB canal-side. Thursdays add the North Yard Night Market with vendors to 21:00. Cap it with the 30-min Regent's Canal towpath walk to Primrose Hill for the sunset skyline view. The main stall areas, not individual shops, set the 10:00-19:00 rhythm — hours re-verified on the official site Aug 2026 (previously listed as 18:00).

https://www.camdenmarket.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1462,51.5414,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Portobello Road Market ★4.5</name><description>Two-mile Notting Hill street market — a world-famous antiques market on Fridays and Saturdays, pastel-house scenery all week.

💷 Free; antiques £5 to £5,000+, vintage clothes £10-40
🕐 Mon-Sat 8:00-19:00 licensed (traders typically ~8:30-18:00); full market incl. antiques Fri-Sat; Mon-Thu limited fruit/veg + household stalls; Sun mostly closed — only Portobello Green vintage stalls + Acklam Kitchen, plus occasional seasonal Sunday openings
🚇 50 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Paddington → Circle/H&amp;C line to Ladbroke Grove, 5-min walk
📍 Portobello Road (antiques stretch: Chepstow Villas-Elgin Crescent), London W11

Ranked last on schedule fit, not quality: the Fri-Sat antiques trading (haggling expected, best dealing before 10:00) is the whole point, and both those days are congress days. A Mon-Wed visit gets a low-key fruit/veg-plus-some-stalls version and the pastel streets. UNVERIFIED: Saturday arcade interiors opening from ~7:00; also whether a seasonal Sunday opening will cover Sep 13 2026 (the market announces summer/winter Sunday runs ad hoc — regular Sundays are mostly closed). The old 'Thu half-day to 13:00, closed every Sun' schedule is outdated per the official site. Longest trip of this list at ~50 min each way — only worth it if he skips congress sessions.

https://visitportobello.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.202,51.514,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>🌯 Street &amp; Casual</name>
<Placemark><name>Padella ★4.7</name><description>London's benchmark cheap-excellent fresh pasta; hand-rolled pici at trattoria prices next to Borough Market.

💷 Pici cacio e pepe £13.50; 8-hr beef-shin pappardelle £16.50; ~£25-30pp with a glass of wine
🕐 Daily 11:30-15:45 &amp; 17:00-22:30 (Sun dinner to 21:00 only)
🚇 30-35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Canary Wharf → Jubilee to London Bridge, 4 min walk
📍 6 Southwark St, London SE1 1TQ

No reservations — join the virtual queue via QR at the door or remotely on the Dojo app (remote joining opens 11:45 for lunch, 17:15 for dinner — join while still on the Jubilee line). Order pici cacio e pepe + the 8-hour beef shin pappardelle. Counter seats solo-friendly; groups over 6 are sent to the Shoreditch/Soho branches. Pair with a Borough Market wander before 17:00.

https://www.padella.co/borough-market/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.091,51.5055,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Blacklock Canary Wharf ★4.7</name><description>The best bookable sit-down within 15 min of ExCeL: charcoal-grilled chops in North Dock, serious value for the quality.

💷 'All In' chops feast £28pp (min 2 people); Butcher Price Monday big chops £8/100g; skinny chops £8; ~£35-45pp with drinks
🕐 Mon-Fri 12:00-15:00 &amp; 17:00-22:00; Sat 11:30-22:30; Sun 11:30-20:00 (last seating)
🚇 15 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line 1 stop to Canary Wharf, 3-5 min walk — the restaurant sits by the Elizabeth line station in North Dock
📍 5 Frobisher Passage, North Dock, London E14 4EE

Book on their site/OpenTable (walk-in space held too). Monday = Butcher Price: big chops (porterhouse, prime rib, bone-in sirloin, lamb rump) at £8/100g all day, but cuts run out as the day goes on — lands exactly on his light congress day Sep 14. Skinny chops piled on charcoal-grilled flatbread is the move; white chocolate cheesecake (£8) sliced tableside.

https://theblacklock.com/restaurants/canary-wharf/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0203,51.5061,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tayyabs ★3.9</name><description>Punjabi institution since 1972 — sizzling grilled lamb chops that justify the queue, at curry-house prices.

💷 Lamb chops ~£13, karahi mains £9-13; BYOB with no corkage keeps bills ~£20-25pp
🕐 Daily 12:00-23:30
🚇 25 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line 2 stops to Whitechapel, 8 min walk
📍 83-89 Fieldgate St, London E1 1JU

Book via the site (ResDiary) or 020 7247 9543, or expect a 30-60 min queue after 19:00. Order the grilled lamb chops (non-negotiable), dry meat karahi, tandoori roti. BYOB confirmed on their site — grab beers/wine en route, no corkage. Loud, fast, zero ceremony. Open to 23:30 daily = reliable after congress days. UNVERIFIED: exact dish prices (menu not published online; ~£13 chops is recent-report level, not official).

https://www.tayyabs.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.065,51.5166,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beigel Bake ★4.4</name><description>24/7 Brick Lane legend (since 1974): hot salt-beef beigels with mustard and pickle for the price of a coffee.

💷 Hot salt beef beigel £7.50; smoked salmon &amp; cream cheese £4.50; other filled beigels from ~£2.20
🕐 24 hours, 7 days
🚇 30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street, 13 min walk up Brick Lane
📍 159 Brick Lane, London E1 6SB

Cash-friendly, brutal queue discipline, no seats — eat standing on Brick Lane. Salt beef + English mustard + pickle is the order (£7.50 per the official site, Aug 2026). Being 24h it works after any congress dinner or before a 07:00 start. Ignore the yellow 'Beigel Shop' next door; the white one (159) is the one.

https://www.beigelbake.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0717,51.5246,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Borough Market ★4.6</name><description>London's flagship food market — worth a dedicated trip for the Kappacasein raclette-grade toastie and grazing lunch.

💷 Kappacasein cheese toastie ~£8, raclette ~£11; Bread Ahead doughnut ~£4; graze lunch £10-15
🕐 Tue-Fri 10:00-17:00; Sat 9:00-17:00; Sun 10:00-16:00; CLOSED Monday
🚇 30-35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Canary Wharf → Jubilee to London Bridge, 3 min walk
📍 8 Southwark St, London SE1 1TL

Closed Mondays — so NOT an option on his light day Sep 14. Crucially, Kappacasein only trades Thu-Sat (Thu-Fri 10:00-17:00, Sat 9:00-17:00), so for the toastie the day is Thu Sep 10 — Wed Sep 16 the market is open but Bill's stall is shut. Arrive before 12:30 to beat peak. Kappacasein (1 Stoney St corner) toastie = Montgomery cheddar + Ogleshield + leeks on sourdough. Combine with Padella (same block). UNVERIFIED: toastie/raclette/doughnut prices (stalls don't publish prices online).

https://boroughmarket.org.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0904,51.5054,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Four Seasons ★3.8</name><description>Chinatown's Cantonese roast-meat specialist — the duck the FT once called the world's best, hanging in the window.

💷 Roast duck on rice ~£13; half duck ~£26; mains £11-18
🕐 Mon-Thu 12:00-23:00; Fri-Sat 12:00-23:30; Sun 11:00-22:00
🚇 30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line direct to Tottenham Court Road, 8 min walk
📍 12 Gerrard St, London W1D 5PR

Walk-ins queue at peak; solo diners get seated fast (reservations recommended for groups). Order roast duck on rice (leg meat if offered) + gai lan in oyster sauce. Kitchen runs to 23:00 Mon-Thu (23:30 Fri-Sat, 22:00 Sun) and the Elizabeth line runs direct from TCR to Custom House — a realistic post-congress West End dinner. UNVERIFIED: exact duck prices (menu prices not published on the official site).

https://www.fs-restaurants.co.uk/chinatown-gerrard-street</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1312,51.5117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Roti King ★4.5</name><description>Cult Malaysian basement by Euston: flaky handmade roti canai with curry for under a tenner — KL prices in zone 1.

💷 Roti canai with chicken/mutton/fish curry ~£8.50; laksa ~£10; card only
🕐 Daily 11:45-22:00 (last table 21:45)
🚇 40 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Road → Northern line 3 stops to Euston, 3 min walk
📍 40 Doric Way, London NW1 1LH

No reservations, walk-ins only, card payments only — queue peaks 18:00-20:00; go before 17:30. Shorter-wait branches: Spitalfields (6 Artillery Lane — 2 min from Liverpool Street, much closer to the hotel), Waterloo (97 Lower Marsh) and Battersea Power Station. Order roti canai (two rotis + curry) plus kaya toast. In-and-out in 40 min; the farthest trek, so bolt it onto a Bloomsbury/West End afternoon. UNVERIFIED: exact prices (menu prices not published online).

https://rotiking.com/location/euston/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.132,51.5291,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Smoking Goat ★4.2</name><description>Bookable mid-price Thai barbecue in Shoreditch — drinking-food menu built around fish-sauce wings and smoked brisket curries.

💷 Plates £8-18; fish-sauce wings ~£10; ~£35-45pp with drinks
🕐 Mon-Sat 12:00-23:00; Sun 12:00-22:00
🚇 30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street, 9 min walk
📍 64 Shoreditch High St, London E1 6JJ

Book via their site (walk-in counter seats too). Order fish-sauce wings, smoked lamb or brisket curry, sourdough roti to mop. Loud, fun, fast kitchen — good for one 'proper dinner out' night; pairs with a Beigel Bake nightcap 10 min up Brick Lane. UNVERIFIED: dish prices (menus are PDF-only on their site).

https://www.smokinggoatbar.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0781,51.5237,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bleecker Burger ★4.3</name><description>Repeat 'best burger in the UK' winner — dry-aged rare-cooked patties, one easy DLR hop from the hotel.

💷 Cheeseburger ~£10, Bleecker Black ~£13.50, angry fries ~£5.50
🕐 Mon-Wed &amp; Sat 11:00-23:00; Thu-Fri 11:00-24:00; Sun 11:00-22:00
🚇 30 min · DLR from Custom House to Canning Town, cross-platform change to a Bank-bound (Woolwich Arsenal) train, 4 min walk — no direct Custom House→Bank service; alternatively Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street + 12 min walk
📍 16 Bloomberg Arcade, London EC4N 8AR

No booking — counter order, minimal seats in the arcade. Order the Bleecker Black (black pudding layer) with angry fries; patties come pink by default. One cross-platform DLR change (Beckton-branch trains from Custom House terminate at Tower Gateway, not Bank) — still a lazy quality dinner after a long congress day. UNVERIFIED: exact prices (site pushes ordering via Deliveroo/Click &amp; Collect without a public price list).

https://www.bleecker.co.uk/locations/bloomberg/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0918,51.5127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>E. Pellicci ★4.8</name><description>Grade II-listed 1900 family caff — the definitive full English breakfast with Anglo-Italian banter thrown in free.

💷 Full English ~£11; pasta/daily specials £9-11; cannoli ~£4
🕐 Mon-Sat 08:00-15:00; closed Sunday (back from summer break since Sep 1)
🚇 35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street → Central line 1 stop to Bethnal Green, 7 min walk
📍 332 Bethnal Green Rd, London E2 0AG

No bookings, cash-friendly, shared tables — the Pellicci family will talk to you. Order the set breakfast with bubble &amp; squeak, or Nevio's cannelloni at lunch. Opens 08:00 and shuts 15:00 (official site), which clashes with congress starts: best as a Mon Sep 14 (light day) or Wed Sep 16 breakfast. Closed Sun Sep 13. UNVERIFIED: exact prices (no menu prices on the official site).

https://epellicci.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0602,51.5271,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
