<Folder><name>🍸 Cocktail &amp; Fancy</name>
<Placemark><name>Connaught Bar ★4.6</name><description>Repeat World's-Best-Bar winner inside a Mayfair grande dame; the martini trolley mixed tableside is the benchmark cocktail experience in Europe.

💷 Cocktails ~£24-28; Connaught Martini ~£26
🕐 Mon-Sat 16:00-01:00; closed Sun
🚇 ~35 min · walk to Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street → 8 min walk
📍 The Connaught, Carlos Place, London W1K 2AL

Officially no-reservations/walk-in (confirmed on the hotel site) — queue forms after ~19:00, so arrive 16:00-18:00 for a seat without a wait (weeknights easiest). Order the Connaught Martini: gin/vodka from the trolley, your choice of house bitters. Dress smart-casual minimum — no sportswear/shorts; jacket not required. Budget one round, it is worth it. Note it is closed Sundays, unlike most hotel bars.

https://www.maybourne.com/en/hotels/the-connaught/restaurants-bars/connaught-bar</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1494,51.5103,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Satan's Whiskers ★4.7</name><description>Bethnal Green classic-cocktail bar with a menu that changes daily; regularly rated London's best actual drinking bar — zero pretence, hip-hop on the stereo, taxidermy on the walls.

💷 Cocktails ~£11-13 — roughly half Connaught prices for comparable quality
🕐 Daily from 17:00; closes ~24:00 Sun-Thu, a little later Fri-Sat
🚇 ~30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Whitechapel → Overground 1 stop to Cambridge Heath → 2 min walk
📍 343 Cambridge Heath Road, London E2 9RA

Walk-ins fine most weeknights; reservations recommended but not essential and taken by phone only — 020 7739 8362. Menu is ~20 rotating classics printed fresh daily — if in doubt ask for a daiquiri or their Satan's Whiskers (orange/gin/vermouth). Best value serious-cocktail stop on this list and the easiest to hit after a congress day. UNVERIFIED: exact current cocktail prices (the bar does not publish a price list online).

https://www.satanswhiskers.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0554,51.5289,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Lyaness ★4.6</name><description>Ryan 'Mr Lyan' Chetiyawardana's flagship on the South Bank — ingredient-led experimental menu, Thames-view room, first bar awarded 3 Pins by the Pinnacle Guide.

💷 Cocktails ~£16-18; happy-hour list cheaper (early evening)
🕐 Mon-Thu 17:00-24:00, Fri 16:00-01:00, Sat 13:00-01:00, Sun 13:00-24:00
🚇 ~40 min · Custom House DLR → Canning Town → Jubilee line to Southwark → 8 min walk
📍 Sea Containers, 20 Upper Ground, London SE1 9PD

Book online free via SevenRooms — walk-ins always welcome subject to space, window tables go to bookings. Menu lists house-made ingredients (e.g. oyster honey, fruit ferments) rather than drink names; staff translate. Pairs perfectly with a South Bank riverside walk from the Tate Modern. Fri/Sat open to 01:00 — one of the later options.

https://www.lyaness.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1073,51.5081,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bōkan 39 ★4.5</name><description>Rooftop terrace on the 39th floor atop Novotel Canary Wharf (bar on 38) — 360° views over the Thames loop, O2 and the City for cocktail prices far below Shard equivalents.

💷 Cocktails ~£14-16; no entry fee
🕐 Mon-Wed 16:00-23:00, Thu 16:00-24:00, Fri 14:00-01:00, Sat 12:00-01:00, Sun 12:00-23:00 (last orders 1h before close)
🚇 ~25 min · Custom House DLR → Canning Town → Jubilee to Canary Wharf → 8 min walk
📍 Floor 37-39, 40 Marsh Wall, London E14 9TP

The 39th-floor roof terrace is walk-in only — no bookings taken, first come first served — so arrive early; the 38th-floor indoor bar has the same view through glass (restaurant is on 37). Open daily, and the terrace still runs in September (it only shuts for the winter months) — weather permitting. Sunset ~19:15 mid-September; aim to be up there by ~18:30-19:00. Smart-casual.

https://bokanlondon.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0206,51.5019,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
