<Folder><name>🍺 Pubs &amp; Dive</name>
<Placemark><name>The Gun ★4.5</name><description>1720s dockers' pub (Fuller's) with a riverside terrace staring straight at the O2 — the best real pub within 20 minutes of ExCeL, ideal for congress evenings.

💷 Pints ~£6.50-7.50; gastropub mains £18-28
🕐 Mon-Tue 11:30-23:00, Wed-Sat 11:30-24:00, Sun 11:30-22:30
🚇 ~20 min · Custom House DLR toward Bank → Blackwall → 9 min walk along the river
📍 27 Coldharbour, London E14 9NS

Nelson reputedly drank here; smugglers' history, blazing fires inside, Thames terrace outside. Drinks are walk-in; book a table via the pub's own website only if eating (worth it — proper kitchen; food served 12:00-15:00 &amp; 18:00-21:30 weekdays). Your default 'one good pint after the congress' answer — everything at ExCeL itself is chain bars.

https://www.thegundocklands.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0096,51.5024,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Grapes ★4.6</name><description>Narrow 1583 riverside pub in Limehouse, in Dickens' Our Mutual Friend; co-owned by Ian McKellen — Gandalf's staff sits behind the bar.

💷 Pints ~£6-7; bar snacks £6-12
🕐 Mon-Sat 12:00-23:00, Sun 12:00-22:30 — no afternoon closure
🚇 ~25 min · Custom House DLR toward Bank → Westferry → 6 min walk down Narrow Street
📍 76 Narrow Street, London E14 8BP

No table reservations (confirmed on the pub's site) — squeeze past the bar to the tiny back deck over the Thames for the best seat. Monday quiz from 20:00 is popular (McKellen has been known to read questions). Open straight through from noon daily. Combine with The Gun for a Docklands riverside pub crawl on the DLR.

https://www.thegrapes.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0341,51.5088,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Prospect of Whitby ★4.5</name><description>London's oldest riverside tavern (1520) — flagstone floor, pewter-topped bar, hangman's noose over the Thames marking Execution Dock.

💷 Pints ~£6 (Greene King); pub food £13-20
🕐 Mon-Sat 11:00-23:00, Sun 12:00-22:00
🚇 ~30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Whitechapel → Overground to Wapping → 6 min walk
📍 57 Wapping Wall, London E1W 3SJ

Turner and Dickens drank here; Pepys too. Tourist-known but genuinely atmospheric — go for the riverside balcony and garden, skip the food if short on time. Walk-in, no booking needed for drinks. Works as a stop between Docklands and Tower Bridge on the Overground.

https://www.greeneking.co.uk/pubs/greater-london/prospect-of-whitby</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0511,51.5071,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bradley's Spanish Bar ★4.5</name><description>Tiny two-floor Fitzrovia dive off Oxford Street — vinyl jukebox, cheap beer, red vinyl banquettes, nothing remotely Spanish. Beloved for 50+ years and its lease newly secured for another decade.

💷 Bottles ~£5.80; draught pints ~£6.60-6.90
🕐 Mon-Thu 12:00-23:00, Fri-Sat 12:00-24:00, Sun ~13:00-20:00
🚇 ~30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Road → 3 min walk
📍 42-44 Hanway Street, London W1T 1UT

Cash-friendly, cramped, all-welcome — the anti-Mayfair; drinks only (crisps and nuts aside). Feed the vinyl jukebox £1 coins (Bowie, Stones, Motown). Downstairs room is the cosier one. Perfect first or last stop of a Soho night since it's 3 minutes from the Elizabeth line back to the hotel. UNVERIFIED: exact hours — the bar doesn't publish them and listings disagree, with Sunday closing reported as early as 20:00; check before a Sunday visit.

https://www.bradleysspanishbar.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.132,51.517,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Trisha's (New Evaristo Club) ★4.5</name><description>Unmarked blue-door basement dive at 57 Greek Street — 1940s Italian drinking den turned Soho institution; fairy lights, photos of regulars, occasional live jazz.

💷 £10 door for non-members; drinks ~£6-9 (simple serves, no mixology)
🕐 ~17:30-01:00; reliably open Mon-Sat, Sunday opening inconsistent — check Instagram @trishassoho before going
🚇 ~30 min · Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Road → 6 min walk into Soho
📍 57 Greek Street, London W1D 3DX

Entry at the doorman's discretion — go in small groups, be pleasant, don't film. Bring photo ID: after a June 2026 licensing review the club kept its licence on condition of ID scanning at the door. Keeps pouring after the pubs shut at 23:00, which is exactly its value: it's where Soho goes when everything else closes. Order simple (negroni, rum &amp; coke, bottled beer). Bring some cash. One of the last true Soho dives — worth the door fee. UNVERIFIED: current door fee (£10 is the long-reported figure) and Sunday opening.

https://www.facebook.com/TrishasSoho/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.131,51.5137,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>🧥 Thrift &amp; Collectibles</name>
<Placemark><name>Classic Football Shirts (London flagship) ★4.5</name><description>World's biggest retro-football-shirt dealer: 1,000+ original shirts on the floor, from £30 bargain rails to match-worn grails, plus in-store match screenings and events.

💷 Free entry; shirts £30-£200, match-worn/rarities £250+
🕐 Mon-Fri 11:00-19:00, Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 11:00-17:00
🚇 25-30 min · walk 5 to Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool St (10 min) → 10-min walk via Wentworth St
📍 Bradbury House, 17 Commercial Street, London E1 6NE

All originals, no remakes. Ask staff to pull rare stock; bargain rails at the back. Store hosts in-store match screenings and events — check @classicfootballshirtsldn. UNVERIFIED: cafe-bar with retro gaming corner and own lager. 10-min walk from Brick Lane, so chain with Rough Trade East, Rokit and the Vintage Market.

https://www.classicfootballshirts.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0727,51.5161,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Brick Lane Vintage Market ★4.2</name><description>The UK's largest dedicated vintage market — 100+ traders in the Truman Brewery basement spanning 1920s glamour to Y2K streetwear, including football-shirt and denim specialists.

💷 Free entry; most pieces £10-£80
🕐 Mon-Fri 11:00-18:30, Sat 11:00-18:00, Sun 10:00-18:00
🚇 30 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Liverpool St → 12-min walk via Brushfield St / Hanbury St
📍 85 Brick Lane (F Block, Truman Brewery), London E1 6QL

Entrance at 85 Brick Lane, down the stairs. Weekday late afternoons are quiet; Sunday adds the surrounding street market but is rammed. Mild haggling accepted on multi-buys. UNVERIFIED: Replay Clothing stall (European football shirts) nearby.

https://www.trumanbrewery.com/markets</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0714,51.5213,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Nobby Lawton's Olde Footy Shop ★4.4</name><description>One of the UK's longest-standing football memorabilia shops, buried in a 1955 indoor market: programmes back to the 1950s, signed pieces, 20th-century kits and vinyl — collector stock, zero tourist markup.

💷 Programmes £1-£20, vintage shirts £20-£100, vinyl from £5 — bring cash
🕐 Market Tue-Sat 10:00-17:30; closed Sun-Mon
🚇 45-50 min · Elizabeth line Custom House→Liverpool St → Overground (Weaver/Chingford branch) to Wood Street → 5-min walk
📍 Wood Street Indoor Market, 98-100 Wood Street, London E17 3HX

Run by Jeff. Stall days can vary — call 07847 174008 before the trek (UNVERIFIED: Instagram @nobbysballs). The market's other ~25 shops (antiques, vinyl including Mike's Record Shop, handmade) reward 30 extra minutes. UNVERIFIED: FA Cup final programmes and obscure lower-league stock as the particular strength.

https://woodstreetmarket.wordpress.com/nobby-lawtons-olde-footy-shop/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0006,51.5843,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Fanatics Collectibles (Topps flagship) ★4.7</name><description>8,500 sq ft global flagship (opened 25 Apr 2025) for trading cards — Topps, Match Attax, Topps Chrome, Bowman; Premier League/UEFA/MLB plus Star Wars, with graded singles and live pack-rip events.

💷 Packs £3-£15, hobby boxes £25-£500+, graded singles £10 to four figures
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 40 min · Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd → 12-min walk down Regent St (or Jubilee Canning Town→Green Park + 8-min walk)
📍 54 Regent Street (Quadrant Arcade), London W1B 4DY

Rip station for opening packs on the spot; hobby/trade nights and PSA grading sessions most weeks (check site and @fancollectlondon). World Cup 2026 card and sticker lines still in flow post-tournament — easy gifts. Sits at the Piccadilly Circus end of Regent St.

https://uk.topps.com/pages/fanatics-collectibles-store</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1354,51.5102,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rough Trade East ★4.7</name><description>The legendary indie record chain's 5,000 sq ft flagship in the Truman Brewery — deep new + reissue vinyl, listening decks, cafe/bar, and free in-store gigs from name acts.

💷 New LPs £22-£30, used/sale from £8; most in-stores free with wristband or LP purchase
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 11:00-17:00; evening in-store gigs run after hours and setup can restrict late-afternoon browsing
🚇 30 min · Elizabeth line to Liverpool St → 11-min walk; entrance on Dray Walk
📍 Old Truman Brewery, 91 Brick Lane (entrance on Dray Walk), London E1 6QL

Check the events calendar before a late visit — an in-store gig either is the attraction or blocks the racks. Listening posts let you try before buying; staff picks wall is reliably good. Two minutes from the Vintage Market and CFS loop.

https://www.roughtrade.com/en-gb/stores/east-london</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0722,51.5216,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rokit (101 &amp; 107 Brick Lane) ★4.0</name><description>Brick Lane vintage stalwart trading since 1986 — no.101 is curated clothing, no.107 is the UK's first dedicated vintage footwear + accessories store.

💷 Most pieces £15-£85; fixed prices
🕐 Daily 11:00-19:00 (both shops)
🚇 30 min · Elizabeth line to Liverpool St → 12-min walk
📍 101 &amp; 107 Brick Lane, London E1 6SE

Better condition-grading and sizing order than most Brick Lane racks — faster to shop. Both shops within 50m of each other, 3 min from the Vintage Market. Open till 19:00 daily, so viable straight after a congress day.

https://www.rokit.co.uk/pages/stores</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0715,51.52,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>British Red Cross shop, Chelsea ★3.0</name><description>London's most famous 'posh' charity shop — Chelsea residents' and designers' donations mean Westwood, Chanel and Manolo-level finds at charity prices.

💷 High-street pieces £10-£50; designer £50-£300
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 12:00-17:00 (call 020 7376 7300 before a special trip)
🚇 50-55 min · Jubilee Canning Town→Green Park → Piccadilly line to South Kensington → 13-min walk
📍 69-71 Old Church Street, London SW3 5BS

Stock turns over fast; go morning-after-weekend for fresh donations. Sizes skew small. King's Road is 2 min away — several more upscale charity shops (Trinity Hospice etc.) within a 10-min crawl. Longest haul from the hotel — pair with a South Kensington museum evening.

https://www.redcross.org.uk/shop/find-a-charity-shop/kensington-and-chelsea</description><Point><coordinates>-0.173,51.4866,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Beyond Retro, Coal Drops Yard ★4.4</name><description>Beyond Retro's largest London store, in a Victorian coal warehouse at King's Cross — 10,000+ pieces of well-sorted denim, sportswear and 1960s-00s vintage. (Their old Brick Lane/Cheshire St shop is closed.)

💷 Most pieces £15-£60
🕐 Mon-Wed 10:00-19:00, Thu-Sat 10:00-20:00, Sun 11:00-17:00
🚇 40 min · Elizabeth line to Farringdon → Thameslink one stop to St Pancras → 10-min walk through Granary Square
📍 Unit 52-54, Coal Drops Yard, London N1C 4DQ

Rag-house-fed stock so prices undercut Soho vintage. Coal Drops Yard itself has one-off design shops and canalside food; 10 min from the British Library. Their Soho branch (Argyll St) is the central fallback.

https://www.beyondretro.com/pages/store-locator-coal-drops</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1259,51.5352,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mary's Living &amp; Giving, Primrose Hill ★4.4</name><description>Flagship of Mary Portas' boutique-style charity chain for Save the Children, on wealthy Primrose Hill's village strip — designer donations merchandised like a boutique.

💷 Most items £5-£40; designer pieces £50-£200
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 12:00-16:00
🚇 45 min · Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Chalk Farm → 7-min walk
📍 109 Regent's Park Road, London NW1 8UR

Priced above a normal charity shop, below resale. Do the Primrose Hill summit view (10 min walk), then the Regent's Park Rd strip; Camden Market's Stables vintage cluster is 12 min downhill — covers the Camden box in the same trip.

https://www.savethechildren.org.uk/shop/marys-living-and-giving-shops/primrose-hill</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1546,51.5399,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Gosh! Comics ★4.7</name><description>Soho's best comic shop, ~40 years in the trade — strong graphic-novel wall, small-press and self-published basement, signed editions and prints.

💷 Single issues £3-£6, graphic novels £10-£25
🕐 Daily 10:30-19:00
🚇 30-35 min · Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd (Dean St exit) → 7-min walk
📍 1 Berwick Street, London W1F 0DR

Ask staff for UK small-press recommendations — the basement is the point. At the Peter Street (south) end of Berwick St; the street still has record shops (Sister Ray at no.75) for a two-in-one stop, with Liberty and Carnaby St 5 min away. Open daily till 19:00, so a doable post-congress dash.

https://goshlondon.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1344,51.5129,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>⌚ Watches</name>
<Placemark><name>Watches of Switzerland — Regent Street flagship ★4.4</name><description>Europe's largest multi-brand luxury watch showroom (Rolex, Patek, Omega, JLC, Vacheron, Grand Seiko + ~25 more) — the single most efficient stop to handle many brands in one visit.

💷 New pieces from ~£300 (Tissot/Longines) to £100k+; Omega ~£2k-15k; Rolex/Patek are allocation-only at list price — no discounts
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 35 min · 5 min walk to Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd (~15 min) → 10 min walk via Oxford Circus
📍 155 Regent Street, London W1B 4AD

Walk-ins fine; book a free appointment online for specific brands to guarantee a specialist. Negotiation reality: zero on Rolex/Patek/hot models, occasionally 5-10% or a free strap on slower brands. VAT: the UK ended tourist VAT refunds Jan 2021 and has NOT reinstated them as of 2026 — the only 20%-saving route is having the retailer ship direct to an overseas address (direct export), meaning you don't take the watch with you.

https://www.watches-of-switzerland.co.uk/store/460</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1387,51.5107,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Watches of Switzerland — Canary Wharf ★4.7</name><description>The closest trusted AD to your hotel (Rolex, Rolex Certified Pre-Owned, Breitling, Cartier, TAG, Zenith) and open to 20:00 weekdays — the realistic after-congress stop.

💷 New Rolex list ~£5k-40k (allocation); Rolex CPO from ~£5k; TAG/Longines from ~£1.5k
🕐 Mon-Fri 09:00-20:00, Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 15 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Canary Wharf (4 min) → 5 min walk through the mall
📍 Unit 22, Canada Place, Canada Square, London E14 5AH

Weekday evening hours fit your 18:00 congress finish exactly. Rolex CPO here is the safest pre-owned channel with full Rolex-backed 2-yr warranty, but priced at a premium over the grey/pre-owned market. Registration-of-interest system for new steel Rolex — as a non-resident tourist your odds of an allocation during a 6-day stay are effectively nil; treat it as browsing.

https://www.watches-of-switzerland.co.uk/store/466</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0182,51.5045,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>David Duggan Watches ★4.5</name><description>The UK's benchmark pre-owned dealer for Patek Philippe and Rolex, trading from Burlington Arcade since 2002 (est. 1976); also an authorised pre-owned Tudor dealer.

💷 Pre-owned Rolex from ~£4-5k; Patek from ~£10k to £100k+; all serviced in-house with 12-month warranty
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-17:30; Sun by appointment only
🚇 40 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street (~17 min) → 10 min walk down New Bond St to Burlington Arcade
📍 63 Burlington Arcade, London W1J 0QS

No appointment needed on weekdays — just walk in and talk (tel 020 7491 1675); staff are genuinely knowledgeable, not salesy. Modest negotiation room (a few %) exists on higher-ticket pieces, more via part-exchange. No VAT refund for tourists (unchanged in 2026). Combine with Somlo at 35-36 in the same arcade.

https://www.daviddugganwatches.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1398,51.5089,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Subdial Clubhouse ★4.9</name><description>London's data-driven pre-owned platform — live market-price charts for every reference — with a by-appointment clubhouse (opened July 2025) in Clerkenwell, the city's historic watch district; the fairest transparent pricing in town.

💷 Market-tracked: Speedmaster Pro ~£3-4k, Submariner ~£8-10k; prices pegged to their own market index, so little haggling needed or possible
🕐 By appointment only — book a free viewing slot at subdial.com; confirm available days/times when booking
🚇 25 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Farringdon (~12 min) → 5 min walk up Farringdon Rd
📍 Lamplighter Works, 49-51 Farringdon Road, London EC1M 3JP

Book the appointment a few days ahead and list the watches you want pulled from the vault. UNVERIFIED: exact slot days/times (weekday daytime assumed) — the booking flow on subdial.com is the source of truth. Because prices track their live market index, this is where you calibrate what any watch should cost before buying anywhere else — useful even if you buy nothing. Every watch authenticated in-house with warranty. No tourist VAT refund applies (2026).

https://subdial.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1055,51.5205,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Somlo London &amp; OMEGA Vintage ★4.4</name><description>The world's only OMEGA-authorised vintage boutique — certified vintage Speedmasters, Seamasters and 400 years of horology including museum-grade pocket watches.

💷 Vintage Omega ~£2k-30k+; antique pocket watches from ~£1.5k; each piece with certificate/extract
🕐 Mon-Sat 11:00-17:30, Sun closed
🚇 40 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street → 10 min walk (same arcade as David Duggan)
📍 35-36 Burlington Arcade, London W1J 0QB

Walk-in friendly (tel +44 20 7499 6526); ask for the OMEGA extract-of-archives on any vintage piece — being the official vintage partner, their provenance paperwork is the best anywhere. Some negotiation possible on high-value vintage. Third-generation family firm (BADA member). Some listings show a 10:30 weekday opening — arrive after 11:00 to be safe. Worth 20 minutes even just to see the pocket-watch cabinets.

https://somlo.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1399,51.509,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Rolex Boutique (Watches of Switzerland) — Old Bond Street ★4.3</name><description>One of Europe's largest Rolex boutiques — plus Rolex Certified Pre-Owned on site; the definitive Rolex experience even though walk-out purchases of steel sports models don't happen.

💷 New Rolex list: ~£4,900 (OP 28) to £40k+ precious metal; strictly fixed prices, zero discounting
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 11:00-17:00
🚇 40 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street → 10 min walk south down New/Old Bond St
📍 34 Old Bond Street, London W1S 4QL

Walk-ins welcome to browse (tel 020 7493 2716); buying a Submariner/GMT/Daytona means joining a registration-of-interest list that realistically requires purchase history — as a visitor, expect to try on and photograph, not buy. Dress smart-casual and they'll happily open cases. Rolex Certified Pre-Owned contact desk on site. No tourist VAT refund (2026 status unchanged).

https://www.watches-of-switzerland.co.uk/store/482</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1412,51.508,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Watchfinder &amp; Co. — Royal Exchange ★4.5</name><description>Flagship of the Richemont-owned pre-owned giant (the most institutionally 'safe' pre-owned buy in the UK), inside the spectacular Royal Exchange courtyard at Bank.

💷 Pre-owned from ~£1.5k; Speedmasters from ~£3k, Submariners from ~£8k; all with 12-24 month warranty
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun closed
🚇 25-30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street (~10 min) → 8 min walk to the Royal Exchange (no direct DLR from Custom House to Bank — Beckton-branch trains run to Tower Gateway)
📍 13-14C The Courtyard, Royal Exchange, London EC3V 3LQ

Book a personal appointment to have specific stock transferred from their vault to the boutique — their website inventory is national, not what's in the shop. UNVERIFIED: booking phone 020 8150 8767 and email royal.exchange@watchfinder.co.uk — book via watchfinder.co.uk if they don't answer. Bring photo ID for appointments. Prices are essentially fixed (Richemont corporate); leverage comes from part-exchange, not haggling. The City is quiet at weekends — a weekday visit pairs naturally with the Elizabeth line from the congress; worth phoning ahead if you must come on a Saturday.

https://www.theroyalexchange.co.uk/watchfinder-and-co/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.087,51.5136,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>OMEGA Flagship Boutique — Oxford Street ★4.3</name><description>OMEGA's two-storey London flagship with the fullest new-collection stock in the city plus on-site servicing — and unlike Rolex, you can actually buy what's in the case.

💷 Aqua Terra from ~£4,600; Speedmaster Moonwatch from ~£7,000; Seamaster 300M ~£4,800+
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street (~17 min) → 3 min walk
📍 451 Oxford Street, London W1C 2PF

No appointment needed (tel +44 20 7907 2566); most references in stock for immediate purchase. Boutique-exclusive straps and the occasional boutique-only edition. Negotiation: list price is list price, but asking politely sometimes yields an extra strap. If vintage Omega is the goal, this + Somlo the same afternoon covers the brand's entire timeline. No tourist VAT refund — direct-export shipping to Israel is the only VAT-free route.

https://www.omegawatches.com/en-us/store/storedetails/7544</description><Point><coordinates>-0.152,51.5137,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Patek Philippe Salon ★4.3</name><description>Patek's own ~1,000 sqm London salon — the largest Patek range in the UK; a pilgrimage stop to handle Calatravas and complications in the metal.

💷 New from ~£20k (Calatrava); complications £40k-£500k+; steel sports (Nautilus/Aquanaut) allocation-only, effectively unobtainable for visitors
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun closed
🚇 40 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Bond Street → 8 min walk down New Bond St
📍 16 New Bond Street, London W1S 3SU

Walk-ins can browse the ground floor; call +44 20 7493 8866 ahead for an appointment if you want specific references brought out — it changes the visit completely. Zero price flexibility, ever. Dress reasonably well. Sits 200m from David Duggan, who sells the same brand pre-owned at market prices — an instructive back-to-back comparison.

https://www.patek.com/en/points-of-sale/europe/united-kingdom/london/patek-philippe-salons</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1411,51.5091,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bucherer — Royal Opera House, Covent Garden ★4.2</name><description>Major Swiss AD (now Rolex-owned) in the Royal Opera House arcade with Tudor and Rolex Certified Pre-Owned — the latest-open trusted dealer in central London (to 20:00).

💷 New Tudor from ~£2,500; Rolex CPO from ~£5k; other brands (JLC, Piaget, IWC) ~£5k-50k
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Road (~15 min) → 12 min walk through Covent Garden
📍 Units 3-4, Royal Opera House, The Piazza, Covent Garden, London WC2E 8HD

Open until 20:00 Mon-Sat — usable after a full congress day when Bond Street is shut. Tudor is genuinely buyable off the shelf here (no waitlist games). Rolex CPO carries the official 2-yr Rolex warranty. Walk-ins fine; phone 020 7952 2040 for appointments. No tourist VAT refund in 2026; ask about direct-export shipping if you want the 20% off and can wait for delivery home.

https://www.bucherer.com/uk/en/locations/united-kingdom/royal-opera-house.html</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1222,51.5124,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>♠️ Poker</name>
<Placemark><name>Genting Casino Stratford Poker Room (ex-Aspers) ★4.0</name><description>The UK's biggest poker room (~30 tables) and by far the closest to your hotel — daily evening tournaments fit a post-congress evening perfectly.

💷 Entry free. Cash: NLH £1/£1, £1/£2, £2/£5, £5/£10; PLO £1/£2, £2/£5. Daily tournaments mostly £20–£160; London Super Deep Stack (month-end); British Poker Series events ~£300+
🕐 Casino 24/7. Tournaments daily, typically 14:00, 18:00 and 20:00 starts; cash games run daily into the night
🚇 20–25 min · DLR Custom House → Canning Town (2 stops) → Jubilee line to Stratford (2 stops) → 5-min walk through Westfield to the Montfichet Rd side
📍 The Loft, 312 Montfichet Road, Olympic Park, London E20 1ET

Rebranded from Aspers after Genting's acquisition completed April 2025; relaunched as Genting Casino Stratford in summer 2025 — same room, official site live in 2026 and billing it 'the biggest poker room in the country', with the London Super Deep Stack at the end of every month and British Poker Series visits. No membership needed; bring passport/photo ID (Challenge 25) and sign up free at the desk first visit. Smart casual, trainers fine. The schedule is published as image posts on the 'Genting Stratford Poker' Facebook page — check it or call +44 20 8536 5630 before travelling. UNVERIFIED: the 14:00/18:00/20:00 start-time pattern, £20–£160 buy-in range, cash-stakes list, ~30-table count, Monthly Cash Race ~£30k / Super Jackpot £50k+ figures, and the 3% gratuity + up to 2% ops deduction from tournament prize pools.

https://www.gentingcasinos.co.uk/casinos/genting-casino-stratford/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0111,51.5442,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Hippodrome Casino — PokerStars LIVE ★4.2</name><description>London's flagship card room: a dedicated 3rd floor (~17 tables), cash from £1/£2 to nosebleeds, in the middle of the West End for an evening out.

💷 Entry free, no membership. Cash NLH £1/£2 (buy-in £50–£400) up to £100/£200; PLO £1/£2+. Rake 5% capped £11; session fees £30–£80/hr at £5/£10 and above. Tournament series buy-ins typically £50–£150
🕐 Casino 24/7. Poker floor Mon–Thu 12:00–06:00; open continuously 24h from Friday noon through Monday
🚇 35 min · walk to Custom House → Elizabeth line direct to Tottenham Court Road (~15 min) → 8–10 min walk to Leicester Square
📍 Cranbourn Street, Leicester Square, London WC2H 7JH

Verified 2026: still branded PokerStars LIVE on the entire 3rd floor, hours and full cash-stakes ladder confirmed on the official site (poker desk 020 7769 8888). Register at the poker cashdesk with government photo ID on first visit (free, 2 min). Join the waitlist remotely via the PokerStars LIVE app — 30–45 min waits are normal at evening peak, so list yourself from the train. Smart casual (neat jeans/t-shirt fine, no sportswear). Monthly 'Our Series'/'Super Series'/MEGA tournament series run in Lola's Underground Casino (lower ground); hosts UKIPT/EPT London legs. Own bar + smoking terrace on the poker floor. UNVERIFIED: exact table count (~17) and the £50–£150 series buy-in range — series schedules publish monthly.

https://www.hippodromecasino.com/hippodrome-casino/poker-at-the-hippodrome/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.128,51.5113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Poker Room at The Vic (Grosvenor Victoria) ★4.3</name><description>London's most storied poker room, reopened July 2025 after a £15M refurb — 24 permanent tables, VIP high-stakes area, 24/7 cash. The pilgrimage venue.

💷 Entry free. Cash games 24/7 from ~£1/£1–£1/£2 upward. Weekly tournaments ~£100–£175: £135 Wed NLH, £100 Thu Turbo, £150 Sunday Grind Turbo; £100k Victoria Championship legs £175+£25
🕐 24/7, every day; cash games run round the clock
🚇 40–45 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line direct to Paddington (~26 min) → 12-min walk via Praed St to Edgware Rd; or Elizabeth line to Bond St + 15-min walk via Marble Arch
📍 150-162 Edgware Road, London W2 2DT

Verified 2026: thevic.com is the official Rank/Grosvenor site, and the July 2025 reopening, £15M refurb, 24 tables and VIP high-stakes area are confirmed (PokerNews). No festival clash with your dates: GUKPT's September 2026 legs are Luton (3–13 Sep) and Leeds (24 Sep–4 Oct), and the Vic's own Victoria Championship legs fall 10–16 Aug and 26 Oct–1 Nov, so the regular weekly schedule applies. No membership — photo ID if you look under 25 (bring passport anyway as a tourist). Dress smart casual: no shorts/tracksuits; 'no trainers' is written but loosely enforced. The Vic publishes its tournament schedule and live cash tables only in the Grosvenor Poker Live app — download it and register before the trek. UNVERIFIED: the exact weekly buy-ins (£135 Wed / £100 Thu Turbo / £150 Sunday Grind) and 888poker LIVE London dates (typically October). Toughest regular lineup of the four rooms.

https://www.thevic.com/venue/poker-room</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1665,51.5176,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Empire Poker Room (Empire Casino) ★4.0</name><description>Small, famously soft 'home-game' room 2 min from the Hippodrome — worth checking both boards; its Mon/Wed 18:30 tournaments actually fit congress evenings.

💷 Entry free. Tournaments daily: Sat £74 (8k stack), Mon/Fri £94 (10k), bounty/Omaha days £114–£134, Sunday £164 (20k stack); Mon Omaha £114 + Wed bounty £134 at 18:30. Low-stakes cash daily
🕐 Casino 24/7. Tournaments daily 12:00 (late reg to 14:00); Mon &amp; Wed also 18:30 (late reg 20:30). Sunday 12:00 event skips the first Sunday of the month
🚇 35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Road (~15 min) → 8-min walk; it faces Leicester Square itself
📍 5-6 Leicester Square, London WC2H 7NA

Verified active Aug 2026 — run by Metropolitan Gaming (ex-Caesars); the full tournament schedule above is confirmed line-by-line on the official site, including the first-Sunday-off rule and the 18:30 Monday Omaha / Wednesday bounty evening events. 80-seat cardroom with its own bar, phone chargers, HD sport screens. Smart casual; clean jeans and trainers fine. The noon starts are useless on congress days but work on your free Sep 10/16; evenings, treat it as the cash-game overflow when the Hippodrome list is long. UNVERIFIED: the photo-ID-for-everyone-after-21:00 door policy — carry your passport regardless.

https://www.metropolitancasinos.com/venues/london-lsq/poker/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.13,51.5108,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>🏛️ Sights &amp; Walks</name>
<Placemark><name>Westminster → South Bank riverside walk</name><description>The single highest-yield London walk: Big Ben, Parliament, London Eye, Thames skyline and Tate Modern in one 3.5 km linear route with a Tube station at each end.

💷 Free (everything is exterior/public; Tate Modern collection free too — open Sun-Thu to 18:00, Fri-Sat to 21:00)
🕐 Outdoor, 24/7; best 17:30-21:00 for daylight-into-illuminations; Elizabeth Tower lit at night
🚇 35 min · DLR Royal Victoria → Canning Town → Jubilee line direct to Westminster (~20 min on train)
📍 Start: Westminster station, Parliament Square, SW1A 2JR

Route: Westminster stn exit 4 (Big Ben photo) → Parliament Square → cross Westminster Bridge (classic Parliament shot from south end) → left along Queen's Walk: London Eye → Royal Festival Hall/Southbank Centre food stalls → BFI → Gabriel's Wharf → Tate Modern (free, and open till 21:00 Fri-Sat — a real evening option) → Millennium Bridge (St Paul's view) → finish Borough Market/London Bridge stn, Jubilee line straight home. 3.5 km, 1.5-2 h. Perfect post-congress evening: Jubilee is direct at both ends; last practical trains back well after midnight. Detour: Leake St tunnel is 5 min behind Waterloo (see separate entry).

https://southbank.london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1254,51.501,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Sky Garden (20 Fenchurch St) ★4.6</name><description>Free 155 m indoor viewpoint over the City, Tower Bridge and the Shard — best free view in London, but ticket release mechanics matter.

💷 Free with timed ticket; walk-up £11.50 early morning (incl. hot drink) / £15.50 evening (incl. welcome drink, DJ); bars no ticket needed (drinks ~£8-14)
🕐 Free visits Mon-Fri 10:00-18:00, Sat-Sun &amp; bank holidays 11:00-21:00; bars/restaurants later
🚇 30-35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool Street (~13 min), then 10-min walk to Philpot Lane; or DLR Royal Victoria → Tower Gateway + 8-min walk
📍 1 Sky Garden Walk (entrance Philpot Lane), EC3M 8AF

Booking mechanics (verified on venue FAQ): free tickets drop every Monday morning (~09:00-10:00 UK, not bank holidays) for the whole week three weeks ahead. Sep 10-13 slots dropped Mon Aug 17 (check for leftovers now); Sep 14-16 slots drop Mon Aug 24 — set an alarm. Weekday free entry ends 18:00, so for congress evenings use Sat 12/Sun 13 (free entry to 21:00) or pay £15.50 evening walk-in (physical photo ID required for evening walk-ins). Backup: book breakfast at Darwin Brasserie — no garden ticket needed. 1-h visit slot, ~25 min queue at peak. UNVERIFIED: St Dunstan-in-the-East ruined-church garden (4 min walk) as the free nearby alternative — normally open daily but occasionally shut for repair works.

https://skygarden.london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0836,51.5113,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tower of London → Tower Bridge → Borough Market walk</name><description>Second-priority greatest-hits loop: castle walls, the bridge, Shad Thames warehouses and London's best food market in ~3 h.

💷 Walk free; Borough Market dishes £5-12; Tower Bridge glass-floor exhibition ~£18 adult, cheaper online (optional); Tower of London £35+ (skip unless keen)
🕐 Route 24/7; Borough Market Tue-Fri 10:00-17:00, Sat 09:00-17:00, Sun 10:00-16:00, CLOSED Monday; Tower Bridge exhibition daily 09:30-18:00 (last entry 17:00)
🚇 30 min · DLR Royal Victoria → Tower Gateway direct (~25 min)
📍 Start: Tower Gateway DLR, Minories, EC3N 1DT; Borough Market: 8 Southwark St, SE1 1TL

Route: Tower Gateway → circle Tower of London moat/walls (exterior free) → cross Tower Bridge on the east walkway → down to Shad Thames (Victorian warehouse canyon) → back west along Queen's Walk past City Hall and Hay's Galleria → Borough Market for lunch (Kappacasein toastie, Padella pasta ~£10-14 if queue short) → Southwark Cathedral + Golden Hinde → London Bridge stn, Jubilee home. ~4 km, 2.5-3 h with food. Market hours re-verified on official site: closed Mon Sep 14 and shuts 17:00 — this is a Thu Sep 10 or Wed Sep 16 plan, not an evening one. UNVERIFIED: exact Tower Bridge (~£18) and Tower of London (£35+) admission prices — both official ticket pages block checking; Tower Bridge ran discounted 'summer savings' tickets to 1 Sep 2026, so check online before paying walk-up.

https://boroughmarket.org.uk/visit-us/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0749,51.5104,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>London Cable Car (formerly IFS Cloud Cable Car) ★4.6</name><description>Cross-Thames cable car with 90 m views of Canary Wharf, the O2 and the Docks — its Royal Docks terminal is a 5-min walk from your hotel door.

💷 ~£7 single / £13.50 return (UNVERIFIED — see notes); 10-trip multi-journey £20 (£2/ride, 12-month validity, sold only at terminal ticket offices); up to 30% off booking online 7+ days ahead off-peak
🕐 Mon-Thu 08:00-21:00, Fri 09:00-22:00, Sat 09:00-23:00, Sun &amp; bank holidays 09:00-21:00
🚇 5 min walk along Western Gateway from the ibis (terminal is on the same street, no. 27)
📍 Royal Docks terminal: 27 Western Gateway, E16 1FA

Rebranded plain 'London Cable Car' when the IFS Cloud sponsorship ended 18 Mar 2026 — maps and signage may show either name. 10-min glide to North Greenwich/The O2. Zero-effort evening decompression after congress: ride at sunset (~19:15 mid-Sep), eat at the O2's restaurant strip or walk the Greenwich Peninsula Thames path, ride back with Canary Wharf lit up. Walk-on with contactless/Oyster on weekday evenings, no queue. The £20 multi-journey (terminal ticket office only) beats singles if you'll ride 3+ times during the week. Night rides Fri/Sat until 22:00-23:00. UNVERIFIED: exact single/return fares — TfL publishes singles only inside its online store and 2026 third-party figures range £5-7; contactless tap-in charges the correct fare regardless.

https://tfl.gov.uk/modes/london-cable-car/</description><Point><coordinates>0.0177,51.5077,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Greenwich Park &amp; Royal Observatory viewpoint ★4.8</name><description>The classic Canary Wharf/City panorama from the General Wolfe statue terrace, plus the Prime Meridian — 35 min from your hotel, ideal for the light day Mon Sep 14.

💷 Park + viewpoint free; Royal Observatory £18 adult online offer (standard £24); Painted Hall £19 (ticket doubles as annual pass, kids free); Cutty Sark £18 — all optional
🕐 Park pedestrian gates 06:00 to ~20:00-21:00 in mid-Sept (dusk-based; posted 06:00-21:00 in high summer); Observatory Sept 10:00-18:00 (last entry 17:00); ORNC grounds free 08:00-23:00, Painted Hall 10:00-17:00
🚇 35-40 min · DLR Royal Victoria (Tower Gateway-bound) → change Poplar → Lewisham-branch DLR to Cutty Sark; or scenic: cable car + bus 129 from North Greenwich
📍 Greenwich Park, SE10 8XJ (viewpoint by Royal Observatory, Blackheath Ave)

Route (half day, fits Mon Sep 14): Cutty Sark DLR → clipper ship exterior → Old Royal Naval College courtyards (grounds free, open to 23:00) → through park gates, steep 15-min climb to General Wolfe statue — THE skyline photo, free, no ticket → optionally pay £18-24 to stand on the Meridian line (book online — cheaper and skips queue) → down via Greenwich Market (street food £6-9, open daily) → DLR back. 2.5-3.5 h. UNVERIFIED: exact September park closing time (Royal Parks posts a blanket 6am-9pm in summer; dusk-based ~20:00 by mid-Sept) — either way an 18:30 post-congress dash for the view alone is feasible.

https://www.royalparks.org.uk/visit/parks/greenwich-park</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0005,51.4769,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Soho, Chinatown &amp; Covent Garden evening circuit</name><description>The efficient West End night out — neon Chinatown, Soho's food streets and Covent Garden's piazza — and the Elizabeth line runs you back to Custom House direct.

💷 Free to wander; Chinatown bakeries £2-4; Soho counter dinners £15-30; West End show rush tickets £25-45 (TodayTix)
🕐 Streets 24/7; energy peaks 18:00-23:00; Covent Garden shops/piazza to ~20:00, pubs 23:00+
🚇 30 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Road direct (~18 min on train); last direct trains back shortly after midnight Mon-Sat (Sun earlier)
📍 Start: Tottenham Court Road station, Oxford St entrance, W1D 1BS

Loop: TCR stn → Soho via Dean St → Berwick St (record shops, Soho food) → Brewer St → Chinatown Gerrard St (Bake, bao and egg-tart stops) → skirt Leicester Sq (skip it) → Covent Garden Piazza street performers + Apple Market → Seven Dials for dinner (Flat Iron steak ~£15, Homeslice pizza £25/20") → walk back to TCR. 2.5-3 km, 2-3 h. Best congress-evening option: single direct train each way, frequent till past midnight. Fri/Sat loudest; Tue/Wed relaxed.

https://www.coventgarden.london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.13,51.5162,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Leake Street Arches (graffiti tunnel) ★4.7</name><description>300 m legal-graffiti tunnel under Waterloo station where Banksy launched Cans Festival — art repaints itself weekly; free, open all night.

💷 Free; venues in the arches (Draughts board-game cafe at Arch 16, Mamushka Polish kitchen, Passyunk Avenue dive bar) pints ~£6-7
🕐 Tunnel 24/7, 365 days; venues inside roughly 12:00-23:00
🚇 30 min · DLR Royal Victoria → Canning Town → Jubilee to Waterloo, 4-min walk via York Rd
📍 Leake Street, SE1 7NN (entrances off York Rd and Lower Marsh)

15-20 min visit — don't make a special trip; bolt it onto the Westminster → South Bank walk (it's directly behind Waterloo, 5 min from the London Eye). Artists spray live most evenings and weekends; everything you photograph may be gone next week. Well-lit and busy till late, fine solo at night. Smells of aerosol — that's the point. Venue line-up verified Aug 2026: Draughts, Mamushka and Passyunk Avenue current; Banh Bao Brothers no longer listed.

https://leakestreetarches.london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1146,51.5019,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>God's Own Junkyard ★4.7</name><description>Europe's largest neon collection — three generations of movie-prop and Soho-sex-shop signage crammed into a Walthamstow warehouse with a bar in the middle.

💷 Free entry; Rolling Scones cafe/bar coffee ~£3, beer ~£6; check site for private-hire closures
🕐 Fri-Sat 11:00-22:00, Sun 11:00-18:00; CLOSED Mon-Thu
🚇 55-60 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool St → Overground to Walthamstow Central → 13-min walk or W12 bus
📍 Unit 12, Ravenswood Industrial Estate, Shernhall St, E17 9HQ

Weekend-only, so your slots are Fri Sep 11 or Sat Sep 12 evening (open till 22:00 — leaving ExCeL at 18:00 gets you there ~19:15 for a solid 2 h) or Sun 13 if the congress day ends early. No private-event closures listed for Sep 11-13 2026 (verified on venue site). 45-60 min inside; phone cameras love it, no tripods. Rolling Scones cafe/bar serves food and drinks all weekend. UNVERIFIED: the yard's neighbouring 'God's Own backyard' taprooms — Wild Card Brewery's website is offline (likely closed) and Pillars' presence at Ravenswood is unconfirmed, so don't plan the evening around the yard bars. Skip if the week gets tight — it's the only far-flung entry here and the journey is the cost.

https://www.godsownjunkyard.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0098,51.5838,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>🎤 Amy Winehouse</name>
<Placemark><name>Amy Winehouse Statue, Camden Stables Market ★4.5</name><description>Life-size bronze by Scott Eaton unveiled on what would have been Amy's 31st birthday (14 Sep 2014) — the one fixed, official memorial in Camden, confirmed in place in 2026.

💷 Free
🕐 Stables Market daily 10:00-late (stalls wind down ~18:00-19:00); statue is inside the open market so viewable any market hour
🚇 40-45 min · walk 4 min to Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Camden Town → 10-min walk up Camden High St/Chalk Farm Rd
📍 Stables Market, Chalk Farm Road, London NW1 8AH

She stands hand on hip with her Star of David necklace — fans tuck flowers into her arm. 2026 accounts place her on the first-floor balcony at the heart of the Stables food-and-drink yard (UNVERIFIED: whether she was re-sited from the original ground-level horse-tunnel spot during market works) — ask any stallholder if you can't find her. Go early evening after congress: crowds thin after 18:00 but the statue area stays accessible. Her Sep 14 birthday falls inside your Sep 10-16 window — expect extra tributes and possibly small fan gatherings that day. No official venue page exists for the statue; Camden Market's own site doesn't list it.

https://www.tripadvisor.com/Attraction_Review-g186338-d15201661-Reviews-Amy_Winehouse_Statue-London_England.html</description><Point><coordinates>-0.147,51.5417,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Dublin Castle ★4.4</name><description>The Parkway pub where pre-fame Amy gigged and pulled pints; signed Amy photos behind the bar, still a working music venue with gigs listed through 2026.

💷 Pint ~£6; back-room gigs free-£15 on the door (most £8-12) — range confirmed on the official site
🕐 Mon-Wed 13:00-00:00, Thu 13:00-02:00, Fri-Sun 12:00-02:00 (CAMRA listing; some directories differ slightly — ring 020 7485 1773 if a late finish matters)
🚇 ~40 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Camden Town → 6-min walk along Parkway
📍 94 Parkway, London NW1 7AN

Front bar is free to enter — the Amy memorabilia (autographed photos) is there, no gig ticket needed. Also Madness's home venue (PRS Music Heritage plaque outside). Live bands most nights, doors 19:15, DJs after the bands Fri-Sun, cheap drinks before 18:00; an 'Amy's Winehouse' tribute band plays periodically (e.g. 22 Aug 2026, £15) — check the gig list on the site. UNVERIFIED: lager-only/no cask ale. Open past midnight every night of your stay.

https://thedublincastle.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1456,51.5375,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Hawley Arms ★4.5</name><description>Amy's actual local — she famously jumped behind the bar to serve drinks; when Greene King had to divest in 2019 the landlords ran a community-backed buyout to keep developers out, and it's confirmed trading in 2026.

💷 Pints ~£6-7; pub food mains ~£12-16
🕐 Sun-Thu 12:00-00:00, Fri-Sat 12:00-01:00 (official site, Aug 2026)
🚇 ~40 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Camden Town → 8-min walk via Camden High St to Castlehaven Rd
📍 2 Castlehaven Road, London NW1 8QU

Music memorabilia throughout — a signed Back to Black sleeve glows behind the bar; head upstairs to the small roof terrace, her preferred spot for privacy. A huge mural of Amy reclining, hand under chin, covers the brick wall round the back of the pub — photograph it before going in (UNVERIFIED: the 'JXC, 2021 10th-anniversary' artist credit). Burned in the 2008 Camden fire and rebuilt ('Camden Town ain't burning down' — her Grammys line — refers to this). 3-min walk from the statue, so pair them in one evening. Booking by phone only: 020 7428 5979; walk-ins fine on weeknights.

https://thehawleyarms.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.145,51.5407,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>30 Camden Square &amp; the Memorial Tree</name><description>The house where she died on 23 Jul 2011 — strictly private (family had it blurred on Street View); tributes go on the memorial tree and railings opposite, by unspoken agreement.

💷 Free
🕐 Street access 24/7; it's a quiet residential square — go in daylight, keep voices down
🚇 ~50 min · DLR Custom House → Stratford → Mildmay line Overground to Camden Road → 10-min walk up Camden Rd/St Augustine's Rd
📍 30 Camden Square, London NW1 9XA (tree on the park railings opposite)

Etiquette matters here: residents fought with Camden Council for years over fan gatherings. Do not photograph into the house, ring bells, or linger at the door — the convention is house private, tree public. Fans leave engraved locks and notes on the tree, flowers and lipstick kisses on the fence; the 'Camden Square' road sign gets signed too. Five minutes is enough. Combine with the Camden Town cluster on your Sep 10 or 16 free day rather than a dark post-congress evening — there's nothing lit to see at night.

https://urban-adventurer.net/amy-winehouse-in-camden/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1323,51.5443,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Amy Street-Art Trail (Mornington Crescent → Camden Town)</name><description>Self-guided walk past the surviving Amy murals — several older pieces are whitewashed; the anchors are Mr Cenz's psychedelic Amy off Mornington Crescent and Bambi's stencil on Bayham Street, finishing at the bronze statue.

💷 Free
🕐 24/7, all outdoors; best light before dusk
🚇 ~35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line to Mornington Crescent → 3-min walk
📍 Start: Lidlington Place (off Hampstead Road), London NW1 — side wall of the Escape bar

Verified surviving stops, south to north: (1) Mr Cenz's psychedelic Amy portrait, Lidlington Place — long-standing; (2) Bambi's stencil 'Amy', Bayham Street, next to the estate agent; (3) the huge reclining-Amy mural on the wall round the back of the Hawley Arms, off Castlehaven Rd (UNVERIFIED: artist/date credit); finish at the statue in the Stables Market. Confirmed gone: the Miller St and Stucley Place pieces were painted over. A rumoured 2024 Bambi 'angel wings' Amy at KOKO could not be confirmed from any source, including KOKO's own site — don't detour for it. Street art churns, so expect one or two changes on the ground. End-to-end ~25 min on foot, ending 3 min from the Hawley Arms for a pint.

https://www.kathmanduandbeyond.com/amy-winehouse-street-art-trail-camden-london/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1398,51.5334,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Amy's Grave, Edgwarebury Cemetery</name><description>Black marble headstone with pink lettering, beside her grandmother Cynthia, in a working Jewish cemetery in Edgware — visitable free, but hours and holidays make timing the whole game.

💷 Free
🕐 Sun-Thu 08:00-16:45, Fri 08:00-15:45, last entry 30 min before close (official site, Aug 2026); CLOSED Saturdays and Jewish holidays — during your stay closed Sat 12 + Sun 13 Sep 2026 (Rosh Hashanah)
🚇 ~90 min each way · Elizabeth line Custom House → Tottenham Court Rd → Northern line (Edgware branch) to Edgware → cab from station rank (~£8, 6 min) or 25-30-min uphill walk up Edgwarebury Lane
📍 Edgwarebury Cemetery, Edgwarebury Lane, Edgware HA8 8QP

The 16:45 close (15:45 Fri) plus your 07:30-18:00 congress days means only Thu Sep 10 or Wed Sep 16 realistically work — allow a half day. Jewish cemetery protocol: men cover their head (bring a kippah or cap), leave a small stone on the headstone rather than flowers, dress modestly, and keep photography discreet — funerals may be in progress. Ask at the office (020 8958 0090) for the section; staff are used to Amy visitors. She was cremated (Golders Green) and her ashes interred here — the family plot is the Winehouse/Levy area. Run by the Edgwarebury Joint Burial Board (Sephardi, West London, Liberal and Belsize Square communities).

https://www.edgwareburycemetery.org.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.282,51.6309,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Jewish Museum London — 'Two Rooms' at JW3 ★4.5</name><description>Reality check: the Camden museum that held the Amy: A Family Portrait exhibit closed for good in 2023; its successor is a small interim space at JW3 (opened 17 Jun 2026) with NO Amy items on display.

💷 Free (some JW3 events ticketed)
🕐 JW3 roughly Sun-Thu 10:00-22:00, Fri 10:00-17:00, Sat closed; expect closure Sep 12-13 2026 (Rosh Hashanah); current exhibitions run to 18 Oct 2026
🚇 ~50 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Bond Street → Jubilee line to Finchley Road → 4-min walk south on Finchley Rd
📍 JW3, 341-351 Finchley Road, London NW3 6ET

Go only if you want the museum itself, not for Amy: the two Sep-2026 shows are 'Legacy' (the J. Lyons family) and 'Tree of Life' (collection highlights, from its 35,000-item store) — the Amy family-portrait material is in storage and no Amy exhibition is running anywhere in London in 2026 (Design Museum's 'Amy: Beyond the Stage' ended in 2022). A £1m government grant is funding a permanent new home targeted for ~2030, likely in the East End. UNVERIFIED: exact JW3 daily hours — check jw3.org.uk before travelling. JW3 has airport-style security at the door — carry photo ID. The in-house kosher cafe is fine for a light lunch.

https://jewishmuseum.org.uk/whats-on/two-rooms/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1784,51.5453,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>⚡ Harry Potter</name>
<Placemark><name>Warner Bros. Studio Tour London — The Making of Harry Potter ★4.8</name><description>The actual sets, props and creature workshops from all 8 films (Great Hall, Diagon Alley, Gringotts, Hogwarts model) — the definitive HP experience, and 2026 is the 25th-anniversary year.

💷 Adult £58.50 direct (wbstudiotour.co.uk); Watford Junction shuttle FREE with ticket; no walk-up sales — pre-book only
🕐 Sep 2026 (official calendar): studio opens 08:30, first tour 09:00, final tour 18:30, studio closes 22:00; timed-entry slots, pre-book mandatory
🚇 ~1h45 each way · walk 5 min to Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd (18 min) → Northern line 2 stops to Euston (5 min) → London Northwestern train to Watford Junction (16-20 min fast) → free electric shuttle 15 min (runs at least every 30 min; first bus 08:15, last 22:00)
📍 Studio Tour Drive, Leavesden WD25 7LR

This is a half-to-full-day commitment: 3.5-4h+ on site plus ~3.5h round-trip = 7-8h door to door. BOOK IMMEDIATELY — official guidance is several weeks ahead and it's anniversary year; weekday slots like Mon Sep 14 outlast weekends but don't gamble. Buy direct, not via resellers (£97+ coach packages are worse value than DIY train). Oyster/contactless covers Euston→Watford Junction. Confirmed on the official site: 'First Year at Hogwarts' feature ends Sep 7 and the Dark Arts event runs Sep 16-Nov 8, so his visit falls on the standard (still complete) tour. Butterbeer + lunch on site are pricey; eat at the mid-tour backlot café.

https://www.wbstudiotour.co.uk</description><Point><coordinates>-0.4177,51.6905,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harry Potter and the Cursed Child — Palace Theatre ★4.6</name><description>The original two-part stage epic plays its FINAL performances ever on Sep 20, 2026 (a reimagined one-part version replaces it from Oct 9) — his stay lands in the last-chance fortnight.

💷 Friday Forty lottery: £40 total for BOTH parts (£20/part); regular seats from £15 per part (premium bands run to £100+), billed for both parts
🕐 Two-part schedule: Wed/Fri/Sat Part One 14:00 + Part Two 19:00; Sun Part One 13:00 + Part Two 18:00; dark Mon/Tue/Thu
🚇 ~30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd (18 min) → 6 min walk via Charing Cross Rd
📍 Palace Theatre, 113 Shaftesbury Avenue, London W1D 5AY

Friday Forty mechanics (verified): enter free in the TodayTix app; entries open Mon 00:01, close Fri 13:00, winners notified 13:00-17:00 Fri, tickets are for the FOLLOWING week's shows — 40 tickets per performance at £40 for both parts. So enter by Fri Sep 4 for the Sep 7-13 shows and Fri Sep 11 for Sep 14-20. Congress reality: matinees clash with congress hours, so both parts in one day = Sunday Sep 13 only; alternatively book Part Two alone for a Fri/Sat 19:00 (doable if you accept half the story — congress ends 18:00, ~30 min door-to-door makes a 19:00 curtain). ~2h40 per part.

https://uk.harrypottertheplay.com/ticket-information/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.129,51.5133,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>House of MinaLima ★4.8</name><description>Free 3-floor gallery-shop of Miraphora Mina &amp; Eduardo Lima — the duo who designed every graphic prop in the films (Daily Prophet, Marauder's Map, Hogwarts letters); the best free HP stop in London.

💷 Free entry; open-edition prints and postcards make the best non-tat HP souvenirs
🕐 Daily 11:00-18:45 incl. bank holidays (timed entry possible when busy)
🚇 ~30 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Tottenham Court Rd (18 min) → 8 min walk into Wardour St
📍 157 Wardour Street, London W1F 8WQ

Ground-floor shop + lower-ground gallery (stairs only to gallery); no booking needed for individuals. 30-45 min is enough. Closes 18:45, so on congress days he just misses it — pair it instead with a Cursed Child Sunday or a free-day Soho evening (5 min from the Palace Theatre; Chinatown dinner adjacent). Staff genuinely know the design history — ask about the Black family tapestry.

https://minalima.com/visit-us/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1348,51.5152,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harry Potter filming-locations walk (Leadenhall Market anchor)</name><description>Self-guided free loop of the real film locations: Leadenhall Market (Diagon Alley in Philosopher's Stone), Millennium Bridge (destroyed in Half-Blood Prince), Borough Market's 7 Stoney St (Leaky Cauldron in PoA), Scotland Place (Ministry of Magic visitor entrance), Goodwin's Court &amp; Cecil Court (Diagon/Knockturn Alley inspiration), Australia House exterior (Gringotts interiors).

💷 Free
🕐 Streets 24/7; Leadenhall arcade officially open 24/7 but its shops/pubs run ~10:00-18:00 Mon-Fri and mostly shut weekends (empty arcade = better photos); Australia House is a working embassy — exterior only
🚇 ~25 min to start · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street (12 min) → 8 min walk to Leadenhall
📍 Start: Leadenhall Market, Gracechurch Street, London EC3V 1LT

Efficient order (2.5-3h with two tube hops): Leadenhall — find the blue-door optician in Bull's Head Passage used as the Leaky Cauldron entrance — walk 15 min to Millennium Bridge/St Paul's, cross to Bankside, 10 min to Borough Market (7 Stoney St, PoA Leaky Cauldron; the market itself runs Tue-Sun, closed Mon — the facade is visible anytime), Jubilee line London Bridge → Westminster for Scotland Place + Great Scotland Yard, finish via Cecil Court/Goodwin's Court off St Martin's Lane. Perfect for free-day Sep 10 morning; the Leadenhall leg alone also works as a 1h congress-evening escape (25 min from ExCeL). (The old House of Spells shop on Charing Cross Rd has closed — its official site now lists only Liverpool and Stratford-upon-Avon; for licensed merch use MinaLima or the King's Cross shop instead.)

https://leadenhallmarket.co.uk/visit/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0836,51.5128,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Platform 9¾ + The Harry Potter Shop, King's Cross ★4.3</name><description>The half-vanished luggage trolley in the station wall with wand-and-scarf photo staging, next to the wand-lined official shop — iconic, free, and queue-managed by pros.

💷 Free to queue and shoot on your own phone; optional pro photo packages sold in-store
🕐 Shop Mon-Sat 08:00-22:00, Sun 09:00-20:00; photo op closes ~1h before shop close in busy periods
🚇 ~35 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Farringdon (15 min) → Thameslink 1 stop to St Pancras (4 min) → 5 min walk to the western concourse
📍 Western concourse, King's Cross Station, Euston Rd, London N1 9AP

Queue reality: 45-60 min midday, worse on weekends. Hack for his schedule: go on a congress evening after 20:30 (Mon-Sat shop runs to 22:00) or before 09:00 on free-day Sep 10 — queue drops to minutes. Staff fly your scarf for the jump shot and take photos on your phone too; buying the pro shot is optional and never pushed. 20-30 min total off-peak. St Pancras's gothic facade (Chamber of Secrets flying-car scene) is directly across the road — 5 extra minutes.

https://harrypottershop.co.uk/pages/kings-cross</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1243,51.532,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tour for Muggles — guided HP walking tour ★4.9</name><description>The dedicated actor-led 2h version of the filming-locations walk (TripAdvisor Hall of Fame) — pay £19 to have the trivia and navigation done for you; departs from Leadenhall Market.

💷 £19 adult; free cancellation up to 24h before
🕐 Wed-Sun daytime departures 09:00-17:00; Tue 'Dark Arts' evening tour 18:30; no tours Mon
🚇 ~25 min · Custom House → Elizabeth line to Liverpool Street (12 min) → 8 min walk
📍 Meeting point: Leadenhall Market, Gracechurch Street, London EC3V 1LT

Only book this instead of, not in addition to, the self-guided walk — same territory. Guides are trained actors; ~2h / 2.4 miles at easy pace ending near Borough Market (Jubilee line from London Bridge gets him home). For his week: daytime slots only fit free-day Sep 10 (Thu) or Sep 16 pre-departure (Wed); the Tue 18:30 Dark Arts tour works if he can exit the congress at 18:00 on the dot (~25-30 min door to meeting point). Skip if he'd rather roam at photo-stop pace — the DIY loop covers the same ground free.

https://tourformuggles.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0839,51.5127,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>⚽ Football</name>
<Placemark><name>London Stadium Tour ★4.4</name><description>60-min guided tour of West Ham's 2012 Olympic stadium — dressing room, players' tunnel and pitchside, plus the indoor athletes' warm-up track — and the closest big-stadium tour to his hotel by a distance.

💷 £22 adult standard guided tour; Legends, 'An Evening With' and VIP tours cost more (VIP includes free drink + photo)
🕐 Most days, timed guided slots — typically 11:00 and 13:00; standard tours limited/replaced by a Matchday Tour on West Ham matchdays — note Fri 11 Sep is a home game
🚇 25-35 min · DLR Royal Victoria → Canning Town → Jubilee 2 stops to Stratford → 15-20 min walk across Olympic Park
📍 London Stadium, Queen Elizabeth Olympic Park, Stratford, London E20 2ST

Book the tour for a non-matchday, then come back Fri 11 Sep for West Ham v Wrexham (20:00) — tour + live match at the same ground in one trip. Dual Olympics/West Ham content; you walk the original 2012 warm-up track. UNVERIFIED: the £22 figure (booking site only reveals price at checkout) and the exact tour start point (previously the ticket office under the Stadium Store). The old '75-min with welcome drink + photo' billing is wrong — the standard tour is 60 min and drink/photo are VIP-tour perks.

https://stadiumtourbookings.london-stadium.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0166,51.5386,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Tottenham Hotspur Stadium Tour ★4.7</name><description>Consensus best stadium tour in London — the £1bn stadium's dressing room, tunnel, pitchside and press areas, ~90 min; F1 DRIVE karting (from £35) is in the same building.

💷 Stadium tour from £23 adult (kids go free); matchday tour from £50; Legends tour from £60 — all confirmed on the official site
🕐 Daily timed slots (typically ~10:00-17:00); standard tours suspended on event/matchdays (a paid Matchday Tour runs instead) — Spurs host Everton Sat 12 Sep 17:30
🚇 50-55 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool Street → Overground (Weaver line) to White Hart Lane → 5 min walk
📍 782 High Road, Tottenham, London N17 0BX

Book direct on the official site — third-party resellers charge more. Combine with the Dare Skywalk (below) in one visit; allow ~4h total with travel. Realistically this is a Sep 10 or Sep 16-morning activity given congress hours.

https://www.tottenhamhotspurstadium.com/attractions/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0662,51.6042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>The Dare Skywalk ★4.6</name><description>Harnessed climb over the Tottenham stadium roof to a glass walkway 46.8 m above the pitch, up to the golden cockerel, with skyline views back toward Canary Wharf — the one genuinely unique stadium experience in London.

💷 From £29; 'The Edge' adrenaline add-on from £10 (both confirmed on the official site); ~90 min all-in
🕐 Timed slots most days (weather-dependent); standard climbs suspended on event/matchdays incl. Sat 12 Sep — book a slot in advance
🚇 50-55 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Liverpool Street → Overground to White Hart Lane → 5 min walk
📍 Tottenham Hotspur Stadium, 782 High Road, London N17 0BX

Briefing + harness at base camp, then the climb up the exposed walkway. Min age 8, min height 1.2 m; under-18s need an accompanying adult; wear closed shoes. Book the climb and stadium tour as a same-day pair to justify the trek to N17. Slots can close for maintenance/events — check the calendar for Sep 10 or 16.

https://www.tottenhamhotspurstadium.com/attractions/the-dare-skywalk</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0662,51.6042,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Emirates Stadium Tour + Arsenal Museum ★4.6</name><description>Self-guided audio tour (multiple languages) through the dressing room, tunnel and pitchside, museum included — the slickest do-it-at-your-own-pace option, good for an odd free hour.

💷 From £35 adult, £28 senior/student, £25 child (audio tour + museum)
🕐 Mon-Sat 09:30-18:00 (last entry 17:00), Sun 10:00-16:00 (last entry 15:00) — published pattern to 5 Sep 2026, expect same after; CLOSED on home matchdays: Sun 13 Sep (Arsenal Women v Palace at the Emirates, confirmed) and possibly Thu 10 Sep if Arsenal draw a home UCL MD1 date
🚇 45-55 min · DLR/Jubilee via Canning Town to Stratford → Mildmay Overground to Highbury &amp; Islington → 12 min walk
📍 Emirates Stadium, Hornsey Road, London N7 7AJ

Self-guided = flexible entry time, no group herding. Walk 10 min east afterwards to Highbury Square — the preserved Art Deco East Stand facade of the old Highbury stadium. Cheaper alternative to touring: £12-18 ticket to Arsenal Women v Palace on Sun 13 Sep puts you in the actual bowl on matchday. UNVERIFIED: the £35/£28/£25 prices and exact hours (arsenal.com blocks automated checks); if the Arsenal Direct link plays up, go via arsenal.com/tours.

https://arsenaldirect.arsenal.com/tour/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1084,51.5549,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Stamford Bridge Tour &amp; Museum ★4.6</name><description>60-min guided tour departing several times daily plus the biggest club trophy collection in London; the most schedule-friendly guided tour since departures are near-continuous.

💷 ~£30-33 adult; museum-inclusive 'Classic Tour' and Legends/WSL/VIP tours also offered; trophy photo-op costs extra
🕐 Daily, multiple guided departures (60 min tour, confirmed); CLOSED Sat 12 Sep (Chelsea v Hull at home)
🚇 55-65 min · Jubilee Canning Town → Westminster → District line to Fulham Broadway → 5 min walk
📍 Stamford Bridge, Fulham Road, London SW6 1HS

Book on tours.chelseafc.com — third-party sites add fees. Photo with the Champions League trophies on arrival (purchase optional). It's the longest schlep from Docklands of the four club tours; only bother if he cares about Chelsea specifically or pairs it with a West London evening. UNVERIFIED: the ~£30-33 price and the '10:00-15:00 every ~20 min' departure pattern (prices only show at checkout); also note the booking site now lists the museum-inclusive option as a separate once-daily 'Classic Tour' — check whether the base Stadium Tour still includes the museum before assuming.

https://www.chelseafc.com/en/stadium-tour-and-museum-opening-times</description><Point><coordinates>-0.191,51.4816,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Wembley Stadium (Express Tour only during stay) ★4.6</name><description>Half-corrected warning: full Wembley tours are suspended for the summer 2026 concert season and only resume 21 Sep — but cut-down Express Tours (no dressing room/player areas) DO run 14-17 Sep, i.e. his last three days. Otherwise it's arch, Olympic Way and the Bobby Moore statue, free from outside.

💷 Express Tour available 14-17 Sep (price only shown at checkout; full tour normally ~£28-35 adult); exterior free
🕐 Full tours CLOSED until 21 Sep 2026 (concert build/breakdown); Express Tours 14-17 Sep, slots roughly 10:00-16:00; Olympic Way open always
🚇 60-70 min · Jubilee direct from Canning Town to Wembley Park → 10-15 min walk down Olympic Way
📍 Wembley Stadium, South Way, Wembley HA9 0WS

Aggregators still sell 'Wembley tours' for dates when only the reduced Express route runs — book only on the official site and check what's included (player areas excluded 14-17 Sep due to event prep). Sat 12 Sep there's a Diljit Dosanjh stadium concert (confirmed; Bon Jovi plays 4/6/9 Sep), so the area will be rammed that weekend. The Tottenham roof walk remains the better icon this trip. UNVERIFIED: Express Tour price.

https://bookings.wembleytours.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.2796,51.556,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
<Folder><name>👜 Burberry &amp; LV</name>
<Placemark><name>Burberry Global Flagship (New Bond Street) ★4.5</name><description>Burberry's global flagship, rebuilt 2023 — the one store with every current line: full trench/outerwear range, scarf bar, leather goods, VIP fitting rooms.

💷 Heritage trench ~£1,900-2,300; cashmere scarf ~£500; full retail — no UK VAT refund (scheme abolished Jan 2021, NOT reinstated as of Aug 2026)
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 12:00-18:00 (re-verified Aug 2026 on two independent listings)
🚇 ~32 min · 5 min walk to Custom House → Elizabeth line direct to Bond Street (18 min) → 5 min walk via Davies St/Brook St
📍 21-23 New Bond Street, London W1S 2RE

Walk-in fine, rarely queues; book a trench fitting via the burberry.com store page (alterations included). If 19:00 is too tight, the Burberry at 121 Regent St (verified open Aug 2026) runs to 20:00 Mon-Sat. Price reality: UK list ≈ EU list, but EU cities refund ~12% VAT and the UK refunds nothing — Paris/Milan beat London at full price. Vs Israel: no Burberry boutique in Israel and importer prices run 20-40% over UK list, so London still wins vs home. 'Direct export' (store ships to Israel, UK VAT off) triggers Israeli VAT + customs — rarely worth it.

https://stores.burberry.com/en/uk/london/21-23-new-bond-street</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1429,51.511,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Louis Vuitton Maison New Bond Street ★4.1</name><description>LV's London flagship in a Peter Marino building literally next door to Burberry — fullest UK stock incl. men's, watches, fragrance, hot-stamping.

💷 Canvas bags ~£1,300-2,600 (Neverfull/Speedy tier ~£1,700-1,900); small leather goods £300-650; no VAT refund
🕐 Mon-Fri 10:00-20:00, Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 12:00-18:00 (verified against LV's official store page)
🚇 ~32 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Bond Street (18 min) + 5 min walk
📍 17-20 New Bond Street, London W1S 2RB

Walk-in with door greeter; weekday mornings walk straight in, weekend afternoons expect a 10-25 min outside queue (they take your name at the door). Appointments via the store page or +44 20 7998 6286 (number verified) — call ahead to hold a specific bag, popular models sell out. UK list ≈ EU list but no refund, so EU is ~12% cheaper at full price; LV has no store in Israel at all, so London is the practical option vs courier/gray-market markups. Israel's arrival allowance is $200/person — above that is declarable.

https://uk.louisvuitton.com/eng-gb/point-of-sale/united-kingdom/louis-vuitton-london-new-bond-street</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1427,51.5108,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Burberry Outlet (Hackney Factory Shop) ★4.0</name><description>Burberry's only UK factory outlet, in its old Hackney works: past-season stock at 20-50% off — the one genuine luxury bargain in London, and on your side of town.

💷 20-50% off retail: cashmere scarves ~£250-350 (vs ~£500), knits/polos £100-250, trenches ~£900-1,400 when in stock
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-18:00, Sun 11:00-17:00 (listings genuinely conflict — Yelp shows an hour later; call +44 20 8328 4287 before trekking out)
🚇 ~40 min · Custom House DLR → Canning Town → Jubilee 2 stops to Stratford → Mildmay line Overground 2 stops to Homerton → 7 min walk
📍 29-31 Chatham Place, London E9 6LP

Re-verified still trading 2026: Yelp listing updated May 2026 and Tripadvisor reviews through 2026; ignore the stale Foursquare 'now closed' flag — it contradicts every fresher source, but the not-on-Burberry's-own-locator status is why phoning first is smart. Stock reality: strong on scarves, knitwear, accessories, kids; classic trench coats appear erratically in odd sizes — treat one as a lucky find, not the plan. Some lines are made-for-outlet rather than marked-down mainline — check labels. Spacious, uncrowded on weekday mornings; card accepted; returns policy stricter than mainline.

https://www.visitlondon.com/things-to-do/place/4194330-burberry-outlet</description><Point><coordinates>-0.0512,51.5465,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Selfridges (LV + Burberry under one roof) ★4.5</name><description>One-stop department store with a full LV boutique (hot-stamping incl.) and a Burberry concession — and the latest-open venue on congress nights (22:00 Mon-Fri).

💷 Same list prices as the flagships; entry free; no in-store VAT refund — a 'ship-to-home' direct-export route removes UK VAT but adds shipping + Israeli import tax
🕐 Mon-Fri 10:00-22:00, Sat 10:00-21:00, Sun 11:30-18:00 (Sun: browsing only until 12:00) — 22:00 weekday close confirmed on two independent 2026 sources
🚇 ~33 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Bond Street (18 min), Davies St exit, 5 min walk
📍 400 Oxford Street, London W1A 1AB

UNVERIFIED: internal LV layout (accessories ground floor, men's 1st, women's + shoe gallery 2nd) — confirmed only that the LV boutique and personalisation/hot-stamping exist; same stock system as Bond St, usually shorter waits. Burberry concession in womens/menswear designer rooms. Free personal-shopping appointments via selfridges.com. Food hall on the ground floor for the ride back.

https://www.selfridges.com/GB/en/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1527,51.5145,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Harrods (Superbrands: LV + Burberry) ★4.4</name><description>The other one-stop: LV in the first-floor Superbrands run plus Burberry men's/women's — pair the shopping with the building itself.

💷 Full list prices; entry free; free Rewards signup gives occasional 10% events (never on LV)
🕐 Mon-Sat 10:00-21:00, Sun 11:30-18:00 (browsing only until 12:00 Sun) — verified vs harrods.com
🚇 ~45 min · DLR Custom House → Canning Town → Jubilee to Green Park → Piccadilly line 1 stop to Knightsbridge (Hans Crescent station exit is directly beside the store)
📍 87-135 Brompton Road, London SW1X 7XL

LV concession queues usually shorter than Bond St; hot-stamping available. No large luggage/rucksacks inside (UNVERIFIED: paid cloakroom at Door 3 — check harrods.com/plan-your-visit before hauling bags). Honest call: if time-poor, skip — Selfridges covers both brands 12 min closer with later hours; come here only if you also want the food halls + Egyptian escalator spectacle.

https://www.harrods.com/en-gb/c/plan-your-visit</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1632,51.4994,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Bond Street (New + Old) ★4.8</name><description>The luxury spine itself: LV and Burberry sit next door to each other mid-street, flanked by Hermès, Cartier, Chanel, Dior and Sotheby's — a 700m end-to-end recon takes 30 min.

💷 Free to walk; everything in the windows is full list price
🕐 Stores typically Mon-Sat 10:00-19:00, Sun 12:00-18:00; street itself 24/7
🚇 ~30 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Bond Street (18 min); station exits land at the north end
📍 New Bond Street, London W1S (runs Oxford Street to Piccadilly)

Do it as one loop with the two flagships: enter from Bond Street station, walk south past Sotheby's (free auction-preview viewings) — note Fenwick is gone, its 63 New Bond St store closed permanently in Feb 2024 — hit LV at 17-20 and Burberry at 21-23 back-to-back, then finish down Old Bond St (Tiffany, Gucci, Prada; Cartier and Chanel are actually on New Bond St) onto Piccadilly — Green Park → Jubilee → Canning Town → DLR is the clean route home.

https://www.bondstreet.co.uk/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1438,51.5114,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Regent Street ★4.8</name><description>The grand curved flagship street from Oxford Circus to Piccadilly Circus — Burberry's historic 121 store, Hamleys, Apple; an easy 8-min bolt-on from Bond Street.

💷 Free; mostly mid-market to premium — a price tier below Bond Street
🕐 Stores typically Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00, Sun 12:00-18:00
🚇 ~35 min · Elizabeth line Custom House → Bond Street (18 min) + 8 min walk east via Conduit St
📍 Regent Street, London W1B

Verified Aug 2026: Burberry 121 Regent St (W1B 4TB) is live on stores.burberry.com with hours Mon-Sat 10:00-20:00, Sun 12:00-18:00 — an hour LATER than the Bond St flagship, so it's the Burberry fallback after congress. UNVERIFIED: reports that Burberry closed ~21 unnamed stores in FY2026 — re-check the locator the week you fly; the New Bond St flagship 400m away is the guaranteed target. Otherwise useful for gifts: Hamleys (kids), Liberty one block off on Great Marlborough St for non-Burberry scarves.

https://www.regentstreetonline.com/</description><Point><coordinates>-0.1396,51.5117,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
</Folder>
